1
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:32,280
That group date the other day was the worst,
wasn't it.

2
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:38,480
I wish something would happen
to brighten up the world.

3
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:41,880
It's gotten dark.

4
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:48,980
What's that?

5
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:57,480
What's that?

6
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:01,040
There's been talk around here lately.

7
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:02,740
UFO?

8
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,080
Hey, Honda!
Don't flatten the grass randomly!

9
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:21,280
Senpai, are we really doing this?

10
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,271
Of course.

11
00:01:22,321 --> 00:01:28,400
You know there've been a string of
UFO sightings around here lately, right?

12
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:32,080
We can't let this business
opportunity slip away.

13
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:34,120
But, well, what if we get caught?

14
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:35,542
Come on,

15
00:01:35,592 --> 00:01:40,300
everyone will be thrilled if
Katsushika becomes a tourist spot.

16
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:43,800
Come on,
we'd better hurry or the night will be over.

17
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:44,560
Okay.

18
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:46,760
One, two, three!

19
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:51,580
Noooooooooooooooooooo

20
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:11,020
A mystery crop circle has been discovered this morning on the Arakawa riverbed here in Katsushika Ward,
where UFO sightings have been reported one after another.

21
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:16,580
Katsushika is now in an uproar over this
mystery that seemingly came out of nowhere.

22
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:24,420
Wow, this is getting crazy.

23
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,140
Alright, let's do this, Honda.

24
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:27,160
Yes.

25
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,020
Welcome to Katsushika, the land of mystery!

26
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,400
To all you mystery crop circle sightseers,

27
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:43,000
would you like to buy some
souvenirs to remember your visit?

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,020
Mystery T-shirts featuring
mystery crop circle designs.

29
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:50,200
Mystery tissue holders
and mystery phone straps.

30
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:53,880
We also have mystery
manju and mystery daifuku!

31
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,200
These are limited items,
available only here.

32
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:04,880
Come on, try the original UFO ramen,
a favorite even with the locals!

33
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:30,160
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes,
yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes...

34
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:32,420
Because it was all over the major news.

35
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,480
Before you knew it, it became a tourist spot

36
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,480
Anyway, let's go on patrol!

37
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:37,060
Yes.

38
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:38,920
Damn it.

39
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,020
Everyone's jumping on the bandwagon,
damn them.

40
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:44,640
Even though I'm the one
who made this crop circle!

41
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:48,260
Weren't the senior officers the ones
who jumped on the bandwagon first?

42
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:49,560
Be quiet!

43
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,160
Alright, since it's come to this,
here comes the second wave!

44
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,320
The American town of Roswell

45
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,420
became famous when a UFO
supposedly crashed there,

46
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,200
so it's no wonder it grew
into what it is today.

47
00:04:01,810 --> 00:04:04,840
If a UFO really showed up now,

48
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:07,200
What's that?

49
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,540
A UFO!

50
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:13,780
Really?

51
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:15,240
No way!

52
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:17,360
Here you go!

53
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:19,800
I can't see a damn thing from here!

54
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,180
Ladies and gentlemen, spectators,

55
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:25,940
we're currently offering everything you need

56
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:32,460
for UFO watching, including binoculars, opera
glasses, and telescopes, at bargain prices.

57
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:33,520
Binoculars!

58
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:37,320
Okay, don't push, one at a time, please!

59
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:44,900
This is more tiring than I expected.

60
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:50,040
Alright,
time to give the customers some service.

61
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,180
Hey, it's an alien!

62
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:54,820
Aliens!

63
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,120
Hey, what about you?

64
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:58,580
Yes, right away. Thanks.

65
00:04:59,060 --> 00:04:59,860
Honda!

66
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,260
Whoa! This is bad!

67
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,220
Hey, wait!

68
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,200
What do you think you're doing here?

69
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,880
W-well, I was kind of asked to do it.

70
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:09,620
Count on it!

71
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,140
Asked by who!

72
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:12,420
Well, that's just...

73
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:16,940
The only idiot who'd think of
something like this is that guy!

74
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:18,340
Hehehehe!

75
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:22,580
Eeeeeeh

76
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:29,020
Eeeeeeh

77
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:31,180
Eeeeeeh

78
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:31,760
Eeeeeeh

79
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:33,760
Eeeeeeh

80
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:34,400
Eeeeeeh

81
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:34,600
Eeeeeeh

82
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,080
Eeeeeeh

83
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,240
Eeeeeeh

84
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:47,160
Boo-boo!

85
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:50,000
Aaaaaaah!

86
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:50,720
Me?

87
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:57,800
I'm Andromeda, so it's fine, I guess.

88
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,860
You idiot!

89
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:04,420
Ryo-kun!

90
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:05,640
Wait, wait!

91
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:06,420
Wait, wait!

92
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:08,050
Wait, wait!

93
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:10,840
Wait, wait!

94
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:11,000
Wait, wait!

95
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:11,080
Wait, wait!

96
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:11,160
Wait, wait!

97
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:17,340
Wait, wait!

98
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:17,760
Wait, wait!

99
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:19,580
Wait, wait!

100
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,400
Wait, wait!

101
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,340
Wait, wait!

102
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:21,780
Wait, wait!

103
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:22,060
Wait, wait!

104
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:24,480
Wait, wait!

105
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:27,780
Wait, wait!

106
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:33,860
We should be safe now, right?

107
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:36,220
Damn it!

108
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:40,380
I thought we were so close to
making Katsushika a UFO hotspot!

109
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:44,360
All that effort for nothing!

110
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:45,720
Dammit!

111
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:10,640
The police box trip is
finally next week, right?

112
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:13,400
I think it's Hawaii this year, right?

113
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:17,980
Chief Ohara went with his family last
year and apparently fell in love with it.

114
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:22,600
That's fine for you two, Nakagawa and Reiko,
since Hawaii's practically like a neighborhood trip for you.

115
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:24,500
But it's my first time.

116
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,840
Ryo-san, it's your first time too, isn't it?

117
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:31,700
Hawaii? I went loads of times as a kid,
on the Joban Line.

118
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,120
The Joban Line?

119
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:36,400
Isn't that just the Joban Hawaiian Center?

120
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:38,440
Same difference, right?

121
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:41,440
Anyway,
Hawaii's just full of Japanese people.

122
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:46,320
That guy's in Hawaii too, isn't he?

123
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:48,160
That guy?

124
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:49,020
Yeah.

125
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:53,900
He was a friend from elementary
school named Tappei Tanaka.

126
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:57,560
Tappei was good at studying, unlike me.

127
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:02,120
But for some reason we got along
well and played together a lot,

128
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:06,180
but when the new term started
after the summer break in third year,

129
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:08,040
he had transferred to Hawaii.

130
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,140
Did he go abroad to study?

131
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:11,800
No, it wasn't like that.

132
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,940
His parents died in a typhoon accident.

133
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:15,580
Well...

134
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,760
But why Hawaii?

135
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:21,100
Apparently his uncle ran
a barbershop over there.

136
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,120
I wonder what he's up to now.

137
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:28,440
Tappei's radio-controlled UFO was really something,
you know.

138
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:31,420
It flew all the way from
Asakusa to Ueno with ease.

139
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:35,980
It caused a huge uproar,
with people mistaking it for a real UFO.

140
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:41,740
Right, if we ask him, we could get a
UFO that looks just like the real thing.

141
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:44,360
This time we're really
going to make a killing!

142
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:48,800
Ryo-chan, you're not scheming
something again, are you?

143
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:53,740
Shut up! We're going all the way to Hawaii,
so what's the point if we don't have any fun?

144
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:57,780
A trip with the Chief is bound to be cramped,
no matter what.

145
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,900
Sorry for being so cramped, then.

146
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,280
Chief

147
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,000
Good morning.

148
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,260
Morning.

149
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:10,900
Ryotsu, you don't need to worry about that.

150
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:15,360
You're not going to Hawaii.
You're staying behind to mind the station.

151
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:16,640
No way!

152
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:21,940
If we all go on a trip,
the police box will be left empty, you know.

153
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:25,940
But you already gave us the okay,
didn't you?

154
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:26,880
No.

155
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:29,360
It's punishment for that
UFO fuss the other day.

156
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:29,980
But that's not fair!

157
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:31,500
But that was...

158
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,620
If you think of the town of Katsushika,
it can be done.

159
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:35,560
I said no, and that means no.

160
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,360
Smooch!

161
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:38,060
Don't say that.

162
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,740
Please, take me with you!

163
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:40,600
Smooch!

164
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,400
Come on, hurry up!

165
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:57,280
What's all this luggage?

166
00:09:57,280 --> 00:10:00,560
They're souvenirs for the people who
looked after us on our family trip.

167
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:05,480
Don't take the souvenirs. Take me along too!

168
00:10:06,260 --> 00:10:09,840
That's why I brought you all the way to Narita,
isn't it?

169
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:13,520
It's not like it's an Ultra Quiz prize trip,
you know.

170
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:15,460
You brought it on yourself.

171
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:17,780
I'll buy proper souvenirs for you,
I promise.

172
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:19,220
Well, let's go.

173
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:22,140
I'm nervous. It's my first time abroad.

174
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:23,200
Oh no, this is bad!

175
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:26,920
If it comes to this,
I'm definitely going to Hawaii too!

176
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:30,640
I'll have them make a Kappe
New Go and rake in a fortune!

177
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:37,360
Where on earth did Ryotsu
go with the souvenirs?

178
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:40,900
Chief, it's almost boarding time.

179
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:44,060
I guess we have no choice but
to give up on the souvenirs.

180
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:47,660
He's really useless.

181
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,560
Mm...

182
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:09,640
Heh heh heh.

183
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:12,560
Truly a sneaky trick to get to Hawaii,
all on your own skin!

184
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:13,100
Ugh.

185
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:13,380
Ugh.

186
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:14,840
Ugh.

187
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:14,900
Ugh.

188
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:16,840
Ugh.

189
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:16,960
Ugh.

190
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:17,160
Ugh.

191
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:17,620
Ugh.

192
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,540
This flight will be taking off shortly.

193
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,720
Please check that your seatbelt is fastened.

194
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:49,340
That idiot.

195
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:09,080
Alright, we've escaped Japan!

196
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,800
Now all we need is operating funds.

197
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:37,691
Ladies and gentlemen,
Tokyo's famous kaminari-okoshi rice puffs,

198
00:12:37,741 --> 00:12:40,560
how about some Iseya doro-yaki?

199
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:44,317
to all of you who forgot
to buy souvenirs for Hawaii,

200
00:12:44,367 --> 00:12:47,845
or those of you who left
something behind at the airport,

201
00:12:47,895 --> 00:12:49,660
please take advantage of this offer.

202
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:53,940
Wow, these are all things
I wanted to bring along.

203
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:57,220
You won't find an in-flight sale
like this in any guidebook, though.

204
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:01,940
Lifesaver. I just left my
souvenirs back at the airport.

205
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:06,520
Customers who are that foolish

206
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:09,860
Yeah, I'll take the whole lot.

207
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:11,946
That's 100,000 yen in Japanese currency,

208
00:13:11,996 --> 00:13:14,480
which comes to 1,500 dollars.

209
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:18,060
I'm pretty sure I bought
it for half that price.

210
00:13:18,060 --> 00:13:21,502
Sir, we're no longer in Japan,

211
00:13:21,552 --> 00:13:24,380
so customs duties and resident tax apply.

212
00:13:24,380 --> 00:13:25,820
Resident tax?

213
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,720
I see, I learned something new.

214
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:31,660
Fine, it can't be helped.
1,500 dollars it is.

215
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:42,240
Oh my, this is bad.

216
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,400
Thank you, that's all I needed.

217
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:46,500
This, this, this is going to lose!

218
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:47,840
Excuse me.

219
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:54,980
That was close.

220
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:59,400
But with this, I've got $1,500!

221
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:01,600
The Chief's a pushover, easy, easy.

222
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,720
Sure thing, you know.

223
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:04,860
Coming!

224
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:08,040
I'm back.

225
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,960
Miss Stewardess.

226
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,020
Yes, what is it?

227
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:19,520
I'm thirsty, so I'd like some juice, please.

228
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,320
Understood.

229
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:25,440
I'll bring it right away,
so please wait in your seat, Chief.

230
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,520
Chief.

231
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:28,500
No, that's not it, Chief.

232
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:43,680
Wow, I actually came all the way here!

233
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:46,820
Aloha!

234
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:49,900
Welcome to Hawaii.

235
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:02,780
This is the first time I've been
kissed by someone other than my wife.

236
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:06,340
Aloha, Swan from Hiromi, Katsushika.

237
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:07,020
And you?

238
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:11,360
School guide Aloha Fujiyama Arne.
Nice to meet you, aloha.

239
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:12,700
Guy?

240
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:15,000
That's a relief.

241
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:17,020
You don't need to.

242
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:20,000
Chief, we should just ignore him and go.

243
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,540
Y-yeah, you're right.

244
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:27,480
Aloha, aloha,
your commemorative photo is ready.

245
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:28,720
Here you go.

246
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:34,760
This photo is embarrassing.

247
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:36,840
When did you take it?

248
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:40,000
If you won't buy it here,

249
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,420
we'll make it into a postcard and
send it to your family in Japan,

250
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,180
and to Katsushika Police Station, right?

251
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:46,960
Stop it!

252
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,000
If a photo like this gets sent,

253
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,160
people will misunderstand.

254
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:53,220
Fine, there's no choice.

255
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:55,720
At a tourist spot, five dollars is cheap.

256
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,280
500 dollars.

257
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:02,820
Once you've got it in your hands,
you can't return it, can you?

258
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:04,580
We'll do it for 1,000
dollars between the two of us.

259
00:16:04,580 --> 00:16:05,700
Chief.

260
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,000
Fine, there's no choice.

261
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:15,780
Thanks for your business!

262
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:20,040
Now I can go see Tappei!

263
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:24,320
Chief, if you dawdle,
it'll just cost us more money!

264
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:26,420
Where are we headed?

265
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:29,680
Hey, hey, hold on!

266
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:32,220
Terai-san,
this is your first time in Hawaii, isn't it?

267
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:35,520
I'll show you around anywhere you like.

268
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,077
Diamond Head,

269
00:16:37,127 --> 00:16:39,860
Pearl Harbor,
the Trevi Fountain, Lovers' Point

270
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:42,820
The Trevi Fountain and Lovers' Point?

271
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,720
That wasn't in the guidebook, though.

272
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:48,760
An old guidebook like that won't do, right?

273
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:52,300
The latest English guidebook,
for 1,000 dollars.

274
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:54,380
But my English is...

275
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:58,333
Mr. Fujiyama,
the Trevi Fountain is in Italy,

276
00:16:58,383 --> 00:17:00,420
and Lovers' Point is in Guam, isn't it?

277
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:01,300
Gulp!

278
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:05,140
That guidebook was just sitting
in the airplane seat pocket!

279
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:06,300
Gulp, gulp!

280
00:17:07,540 --> 00:17:12,320
You! So you really are a con man who preys on tourists!
Give me my money back!

281
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:12,780
Whoa!

282
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:14,240
Whoa!

283
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,880
Hey, wait!

284
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:17,600
Whoa!

285
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:18,360
Whoa!

286
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,020
Whoa!

287
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:20,200
Whoa!

288
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:20,740
Whoa!

289
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:21,960
Con man!

290
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:22,880
Whoa!

291
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:25,240
Budd!

292
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:42,820
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

293
00:17:42,820 --> 00:18:07,180
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa

294
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:08,480
Hey, you're crashing into way too much!

295
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:11,340
That's him! Catch him!

296
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:12,440
Gah!

297
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:15,240
Uh-oh!

298
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:25,600
Perfect timing! Lend me that bicycle!

299
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:27,040
No way!

300
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:29,300
Please, use this!

301
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:30,300
Yes!

302
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:33,540
Yes!

303
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:33,640
Why?

304
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:36,560
He's not all there!

305
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:37,940
Haaa!

306
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:47,760
Why are there so many patrol cars coming?!

307
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:11,620
Aaaaaaah!

308
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:14,540
Aaaaaaah!

309
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:23,180
Aaaaaaah!

310
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:23,700
Aaaaaaah!

311
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:23,760
Aaaaaaah!

312
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:28,220
Aaaaaaah!

313
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:29,480
So they came after the culprit!

314
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:32,820
They didn't come after the culprit.
Aren't we the ones being chased?

315
00:19:33,100 --> 00:19:35,780
What? Those are the Hawaiian mafia!

316
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,800
Please! Fly!

317
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,840
Alright, hold on tight!

318
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:52,460
Yes!

319
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:57,640
This isn't a circus, you know!

320
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:09,260
Being chased by police cars is so thrilling.

321
00:20:09,260 --> 00:20:11,160
I've always wanted to try it.

322
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:14,180
Glad to hear it.

323
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:17,620
Mister, you're not really a bank
robber or something, are you?

324
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:19,580
I told you, I'm not.

325
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:23,500
I'm a Japanese police officer,
Senior Patrol Officer Kankichi Ryotsu.

326
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:27,540
Got it. I'll just pretend that's the case.

327
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:30,740
So, where do you want to go?

328
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:32,860
Let me think.

329
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:37,120
If we're going anywhere, take me to a town
called Hilo on the Big Island of Hawaii.

330
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:37,960
Hilo?

331
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,160
Too much to ask?

332
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:41,440
No, that's perfect.

333
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:44,560
Hilo's the town I was born in.

334
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:50,600
What's your name?

335
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:51,600
I'm Mina.

336
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,380
So you're Japanese, mister?

337
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:53,900
Yeah.

338
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:56,380
My dad's Japanese too.

339
00:20:57,120 --> 00:20:58,280
I see.

340
00:20:58,280 --> 00:21:00,100
So, have you ever been to Japan?

341
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,040
No, I haven't.

342
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:02,640
It's a great place.

343
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:05,140
Next time, have your dad take you.

344
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:05,880
No way.

345
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:09,120
My dad died before I was born.

346
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:15,420
I only know him from photos.
My mom died when I was in kindergarten, too.

347
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:18,500
Sorry to hear that.

348
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:22,220
No, it's fine.
Honestly, it's easier without parents.

349
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:24,600
Plus, you get to fly around freely.

350
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:26,720
I don't rob banks, though.

351
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:29,740
Hey, I keep telling you, I'm not a robber!

352
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:38,520
So this is Hilo town.

353
00:21:39,180 --> 00:21:41,420
Unlike those rules,
it's peaceful here, which is nice.

354
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:45,100
Apparently it used to be the
second-largest town in Hawaii.

355
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:49,120
Look, it's Hilo Airport.

356
00:21:52,820 --> 00:21:54,780
Oh no, police cars!

357
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:58,200
Sorry, everyone,
but could you let me off here?

358
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,260
Here.

359
00:22:03,420 --> 00:22:05,200
A taxi just arrived.

360
00:22:05,860 --> 00:22:07,440
Everyone, come closer.

361
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:14,200
Isn't that Kam-Kam's taxi?

362
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:17,160
Thanks for looking after me, everyone.

363
00:22:17,820 --> 00:22:19,280
You're really getting off here?

364
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:20,100
Yeah.

365
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:22,260
Bye then, Kōtō-san.

366
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:37,100
I've told you already, I'm not a robber!

367
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:49,740
Do you know about "Tatakai Hazute"?

368
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:53,200
Are you an acquaintance of Lucky-san?

369
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:55,160
Lucky-san.

370
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:10,620
Tappei's childhood friend!

371
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:14,880
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu. We were together in
Asakusa until the third year of elementary school.

372
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:17,140
all the way from Japan.

373
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:19,760
Yes, Tappei, UFO... no,

374
00:23:19,810 --> 00:23:22,660
I just came to Honolulu for sightseeing.

375
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:26,340
I'm sorry, you came all this way, but

376
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:29,900
Tappei died fifteen years ago.

377
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,200
It's just a photo.

378
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:36,840
That's definitely Tappei.

379
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:39,640
You can still see traces
of his childhood face.

380
00:23:40,540 --> 00:23:40,980
I see.

381
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:43,400
Still, that's a shame.

382
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:45,680
To not even be able to
see the grown-up Tappei

383
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,600
except in photos...

384
00:23:48,060 --> 00:23:50,180
Tappei was at the University of Hawaii,

385
00:23:50,180 --> 00:23:51,800
and he married Cathy,

386
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:53,040
a classmate of his there.

387
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:55,420
Then he was soon called up by NASA.

388
00:23:55,420 --> 00:23:58,820
NASA? What kind of work was he doing?

389
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:02,580
It's classified or something,
so I don't really know.

390
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:08,880
I heard he died in an
accident during his research.

391
00:24:13,380 --> 00:24:18,564
Right after Tappei went to NASA,

392
00:24:18,614 --> 00:24:23,500
Cathy gave birth to a daughter,

393
00:24:24,380 --> 00:24:26,480
but Tappei never knew about it.

394
00:24:27,080 --> 00:24:28,500
Tappei had a daughter?

395
00:24:29,580 --> 00:24:31,460
The photo next to that...

396
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,100
Cathy also passed away from illness,

397
00:24:35,660 --> 00:24:38,280
but their daughter Mina grew up healthy.

398
00:24:39,420 --> 00:24:40,680
This girl is Mina?

399
00:24:41,120 --> 00:24:43,620
I just rode in her Cessna.

400
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:44,800
I see.

401
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:50,920
Mina works for an airline run
by my friend Happy Tonoyama.

402
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:52,580
Happy Tonoyama.

403
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:53,800
Ryotsu-san,

404
00:24:53,800 --> 00:24:56,340
if it's all right, could you also tell Mina

405
00:24:56,340 --> 00:25:00,060
stories of Tappei's childhood?

406
00:25:01,460 --> 00:25:04,020
I'm sure she'd be delighted.

407
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,420
Looks like they're having fun.

408
00:25:31,420 --> 00:25:32,900
The Chief and Hirai-san.

409
00:25:36,260 --> 00:25:36,820
Monon.

410
00:25:45,340 --> 00:25:49,060
Flying awfully low, isn't it? Doesn't
look like a sightseeing chopper, though.

411
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:53,920
Could be paparazzi. A Hollywood
star staying incognito at some hotel.

412
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:54,820
Isn't it just hovering?

413
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:07,140
Hello! Is anyone there?

414
00:26:12,540 --> 00:26:15,820
It's a Zero fighter, and a Model 21 at that!

415
00:26:15,820 --> 00:26:18,640
I've built one as a model kit before,
you know.

416
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:19,620
Oof, there we go.

417
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:22,980
This is a replica that looks
just like the real thing.

418
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:30,420
So you're Mr. Ryotsu?

419
00:26:30,420 --> 00:26:32,400
I'm Yama, Happy's man.

420
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:35,020
Lucky told me all about you.

421
00:26:35,620 --> 00:26:37,360
Don't scare me like that.

422
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:40,820
I thought they'd even replicated the
spirits of the war dead in the Pacific!

423
00:26:42,900 --> 00:26:45,400
But this isn't a replica at all.

424
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:47,840
It's a relic the Japanese
military left behind.

425
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:49,220
It's the real thing?

426
00:26:49,220 --> 00:26:51,320
Does this thing actually fly?

427
00:26:51,820 --> 00:26:54,780
Of course it does.
It's properly maintained, you know.

428
00:26:56,240 --> 00:27:00,380
How about a quick hop over to Pearl Harbor?

429
00:27:00,930 --> 00:27:02,200
No thanks, I'll pass.

430
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:05,400
Actually, I came here to see Mina.

431
00:27:05,980 --> 00:27:07,680
You just missed her.

432
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:11,380
Mina's already gone to get
ready for the dinner show.

433
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:12,520
Dinner show?

434
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:18,280
Yeah, if you join the sunset
cruise leaving from Pier 8 tonight,

435
00:27:18,280 --> 00:27:20,620
you can hear Mina sing!

436
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:36,460
I thought it was some kind of sunset cruise,

437
00:27:36,460 --> 00:27:39,560
so it's basically a banquet on a ship

438
00:27:41,740 --> 00:27:42,180
No,

439
00:27:42,180 --> 00:27:44,880
Sir, dressed like that,

440
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:46,840
It's fine, it's fine.

441
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:50,680
It's definitely on a different
scale from the Tachibana-maru.

442
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:53,960
Oh no, Chief!

443
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:56,000
Why are you here?

444
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:59,760
Even the guidebook gives
this cruise five stars.

445
00:27:59,760 --> 00:28:01,460
What a lovely atmosphere.

446
00:28:03,100 --> 00:28:05,019
I'm really glad we came to Hawaii.

447
00:28:05,069 --> 00:28:07,180
Too bad Ryotsu didn't come along.

448
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:07,840
Heh!

449
00:28:08,580 --> 00:28:09,240
Chief?

450
00:28:09,520 --> 00:28:12,530
No, since Ryotsu isn't here,

451
00:28:12,580 --> 00:28:15,640
we can enjoy this trip without worry.

452
00:28:17,540 --> 00:28:20,980
Speaking of trouble,
there's only that con man Fujiyama, right?

453
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:25,404
Right, right.
About Fujiyama, I filed a complaint,

454
00:28:25,454 --> 00:28:28,200
and the Honolulu police have
put him on the wanted list.

455
00:28:29,020 --> 00:28:31,980
Damn it, the Chief, always meddling!

456
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:43,800
Good evening, everyone,
and welcome to the sunset cruise.

457
00:28:45,320 --> 00:28:46,780
I'm Lucky Tanaka.

458
00:28:48,300 --> 00:28:49,960
I'm Happy Tonoyama.

459
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:53,460
I'm Kamu-Kamu Naito.

460
00:28:54,540 --> 00:28:57,840
We're Lucky Tanaka and Happy Kamu-Kamu.

461
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:02,900
Lucky and Happy,
plus the taxi driver, right?

462
00:29:07,140 --> 00:29:08,200
Aloha!

463
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:10,720
Good evening, everyone. I'm Mina.

464
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:13,720
Tonight,
a lovely dinner and the light of the moon.

465
00:29:14,700 --> 00:29:17,900
And please enjoy my sweet song.

466
00:29:19,140 --> 00:29:19,920
Mina

467
00:29:26,540 --> 00:29:31,520
I want to see you,
I can't see you, longing to see you

468
00:29:33,100 --> 00:29:37,540
gazing up at the stars in the night sky

469
00:29:38,700 --> 00:29:40,960
Not bad, isn't that a pretty good voice?

470
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:44,760
Good thing we didn't bring
Ryotsu along after all.

471
00:29:44,760 --> 00:29:51,080
Even our brilliance is truly apart.

472
00:29:52,580 --> 00:29:56,240
Impressive. Tappei would've been
delighted if he were still alive.

473
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:59,020
like the waves

474
00:29:59,540 --> 00:30:05,960
thinking only of you

475
00:30:06,590 --> 00:30:09,520
the melody I sing

476
00:30:09,590 --> 00:30:11,680
tonight too

477
00:30:15,760 --> 00:30:18,180
Missing you baby

478
00:30:18,180 --> 00:30:21,060
Missing you baby

479
00:30:21,060 --> 00:30:22,000
No way...

480
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:25,400
Still in my heart

481
00:30:27,660 --> 00:30:29,640
your voice

482
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:31,080
Miss you, baby

483
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:33,100
Miss you, baby

484
00:30:33,100 --> 00:30:36,380
It's me, Ryotsu Kankichi!

485
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:37,700
Kankichi

486
00:30:37,700 --> 00:30:39,640
Tappei, you're alive?

487
00:30:39,640 --> 00:30:42,280
Miss you

488
00:30:48,380 --> 00:30:50,940
Hey, wait! Why are you running away?

489
00:30:53,440 --> 00:30:54,240
What the...!

490
00:31:03,520 --> 00:31:06,460
This attraction isn't in the guidebook!

491
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:16,000
There he is!

492
00:31:16,050 --> 00:31:18,380
Tappei!

493
00:31:24,860 --> 00:31:25,880
Tappei!

494
00:31:26,360 --> 00:31:27,120
Tappei?

495
00:31:38,820 --> 00:31:42,060
Eeeeeeeh!

496
00:31:42,060 --> 00:31:57,660
!

497
00:31:57,660 --> 00:31:58,740
Do it!

498
00:31:59,900 --> 00:32:00,680
Take this!

499
00:32:06,160 --> 00:32:08,840
It's a grenade!
And the pin's already pulled!

500
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:11,460
Boo!

501
00:32:17,900 --> 00:32:18,820
Pass it!

502
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:20,140
Hurry, Hina!

503
00:32:20,420 --> 00:32:21,000
Over here!

504
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:24,400
Where's everyone?

505
00:32:28,660 --> 00:32:29,660
Aaaaaah!

506
00:32:29,660 --> 00:32:30,700
Aaaaaah!

507
00:32:30,700 --> 00:32:31,140
Aaaaaah!

508
00:32:31,140 --> 00:32:31,600
Aaaaaah!

509
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:32,900
Aaaaaah!

510
00:32:34,500 --> 00:32:36,780
You there!
What do you plan to do about the troops?

511
00:32:37,600 --> 00:32:38,440
Kankichi!

512
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:44,440
Hurry up! Yes!

513
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:47,140
Kankichi!
The Hiryu-maru is going to scatter!

514
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:49,240
Hiryu-maru!?

515
00:32:51,520 --> 00:32:52,380
I won't let him get away!

516
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:54,320
Wait!

517
00:32:55,860 --> 00:32:56,580
Got it?

518
00:33:06,620 --> 00:33:07,780
Something came out.

519
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:11,760
Tappei... could it be that

520
00:33:12,580 --> 00:33:14,680
that man is my dad.

521
00:33:15,780 --> 00:33:17,400
That's right, Tappei is alive.

522
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:18,720
He isn't dead at all.

523
00:33:19,520 --> 00:33:21,500
So after all, Uncle

524
00:33:22,060 --> 00:33:23,420
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu.

525
00:33:23,420 --> 00:33:25,300
I'm Tappei's childhood friend.

526
00:33:26,620 --> 00:33:27,380
Dad...

527
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:28,980
Dad is alive.

528
00:33:46,140 --> 00:33:47,500
What is going on?

529
00:33:47,820 --> 00:33:49,600
Where did they take Dad?

530
00:33:50,020 --> 00:33:51,160
I don't know either.

531
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:54,440
All he said was that
Hiryumaru was going to go wild.

532
00:33:55,100 --> 00:33:55,920
Hiryumaru?

533
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:58,920
Kankichi! Hiryumaru's going to go wild!

534
00:33:59,720 --> 00:34:01,780
It's written
"dragon flies," which is Hiryumaru.

535
00:34:02,100 --> 00:34:06,280
It's the name Tappei gave the radio-controlled
UFO he built when he was a kid.

536
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,880
A UFO? A radio-controlled one?

537
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:12,080
But what does it mean
that it's going to go wild?

538
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:15,920
This is the Honolulu police.

539
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:19,800
Anyway, we have to rescue Tappei.

540
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:21,300
It has nothing to do with me.

541
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:25,620
I'm saying it's none of my business, even if you call me
"Dad" now.

542
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:26,580
Mina?

543
00:34:27,220 --> 00:34:29,700
But I was told Dad was dead.

544
00:34:29,700 --> 00:34:33,600
He never held me,
and he never celebrated my birthday.

545
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:36,580
Tappei must have had some reason.

546
00:34:37,080 --> 00:34:39,500
After leaving me alone for fifteen years,
and now...

547
00:34:39,500 --> 00:34:42,960
Besides, you did this dangerous thing
just because you wanted to see Tappei.

548
00:34:44,520 --> 00:34:46,520
No, it's not like that!

549
00:34:47,020 --> 00:34:50,180
Police as they are! Rest easy now!

550
00:34:50,980 --> 00:34:51,900
Don't be so stubborn!

551
00:34:52,100 --> 00:34:53,340
I'm not being stubborn!

552
00:34:53,340 --> 00:34:54,140
Mina!

553
00:34:54,560 --> 00:34:56,660
I've been living on my own all this time.

554
00:34:57,120 --> 00:34:57,820
So what?

555
00:34:58,560 --> 00:35:00,340
I don't need a dad now.

556
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:03,980
That's not true! He's your only father!

557
00:35:04,300 --> 00:35:05,680
It's not a small thing!

558
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:08,760
Tappei came all this way just to see you!

559
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,900
Then why didn't he come until now?!

560
00:35:11,140 --> 00:35:13,180
That means there was some reason!

561
00:35:13,540 --> 00:35:14,940
It has nothing to do with me!

562
00:35:15,360 --> 00:35:19,020
You have to help Tappei!
You might be the only one who can!

563
00:35:19,320 --> 00:35:21,880
You might be the only one
in the whole world who can!

564
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:26,400
Sorry to interrupt,

565
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:29,600
but did you see the
person who sank the ship?

566
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:30,400
That one.

567
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:31,500
This man.

568
00:35:31,500 --> 00:35:34,200
He's the culprit.

569
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:34,640
What?

570
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:37,520
No, that's not right!

571
00:35:37,520 --> 00:35:39,920
Someone tell them it's a joke!

572
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:41,500
Since when?

573
00:35:41,940 --> 00:35:43,020
Help me!

574
00:35:46,060 --> 00:35:46,460
What?

575
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:48,540
Fujiyama has been arrested.

576
00:35:49,340 --> 00:35:51,280
Apparently he was found floating in the sea,

577
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:54,020
and now they're making him out
to be the one who sank the ship.

578
00:35:54,020 --> 00:35:55,040
What?!

579
00:35:55,540 --> 00:35:58,240
Weren't the ones who sank
the ship someone else?

580
00:35:58,980 --> 00:36:00,500
That's why they're asking Chief Ohara

581
00:36:00,500 --> 00:36:03,480
to be his guarantor.

582
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:05,300
Don't be ridiculous!

583
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:06,920
I'm the victim here!

584
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:08,240
Why would I vouch for

585
00:36:08,240 --> 00:36:08,900
I already told you, he's not the one!

586
00:36:09,520 --> 00:36:11,780
I didn't sink the ship!

587
00:36:12,380 --> 00:36:15,260
Chief, help me, won't you!

588
00:36:15,260 --> 00:36:16,100
Ryo-san!

589
00:36:16,100 --> 00:36:18,060
Ryo-san!

590
00:36:18,060 --> 00:36:21,080
So Fujiyama was actually your senior

591
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:23,260
I'm not surprised, but I'm appalled.

592
00:36:23,260 --> 00:36:24,320
Chief.

593
00:36:25,080 --> 00:36:26,620
Mr. Ohara.

594
00:36:26,620 --> 00:36:29,820
Fujiyama says he's an acquaintance of yours.

595
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:32,660
I have no acquaintances who are con men.

596
00:36:32,660 --> 00:36:33,200
No way.

597
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:34,660
Understood.

598
00:36:35,120 --> 00:36:36,720
Then we'll take him into custody.

599
00:36:36,720 --> 00:36:38,780
Chief, you're cold.

600
00:36:38,780 --> 00:36:42,780
You've forgotten the streets of Kameari we walked together,
haven't you?

601
00:36:45,180 --> 00:36:46,900
Is that really all right, Chief?

602
00:36:49,600 --> 00:36:51,720
It's a disgrace to the Japanese police,
after all.

603
00:36:54,420 --> 00:36:55,980
Why did you lie?

604
00:36:55,980 --> 00:36:57,420
Saying Papa was dead...

605
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:00,200
It wasn't a lie.

606
00:37:00,560 --> 00:37:02,380
Cathy and I both...

607
00:37:02,380 --> 00:37:05,420
We really thought Tappei was dead.

608
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:08,220
So Papa deceived everyone?

609
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:10,540
Deceived? Don't say that...

610
00:37:10,540 --> 00:37:11,760
Well, isn't that what it is?

611
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:13,040
Mina.

612
00:37:13,560 --> 00:37:14,600
Actually, yesterday...

613
00:37:14,600 --> 00:37:17,900
someone went and left
flowers on Cathy's grave.

614
00:37:19,340 --> 00:37:21,380
It must have been Tappei.

615
00:37:21,380 --> 00:37:24,400
He must have had his reasons.

616
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:34,360
We got lost again

617
00:37:35,120 --> 00:37:37,600
Let's ask at that factory.

618
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:43,220
Excuse me, is there a small company
around here called Tomodao Kogyo?

619
00:37:43,220 --> 00:37:45,220
What do you want?

620
00:37:45,620 --> 00:37:48,920
I just came to ask for directions,
that's all.

621
00:37:58,260 --> 00:37:59,520
Help me, you guys!

622
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:03,580
What are you talking about?
This is the police station.

623
00:38:06,940 --> 00:38:10,802
Ryotsu suddenly leaves us to mind
the station and goes off to Hawaii,

624
00:38:10,852 --> 00:38:13,460
he'd better at least bring back a souvenir.

625
00:38:15,820 --> 00:38:18,740
Well, when you think of Hawaii,
it's macadamia nuts, I'd guess.

626
00:38:19,780 --> 00:38:20,920
What are you saying?

627
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:23,040
When you think of Hawaii, it's Agnes Lum!

628
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:25,140
What's that supposed to mean?

629
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:27,360
You don't even know Agnes Lum?

630
00:38:31,600 --> 00:38:32,480
This, this is it!

631
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:35,960
Th-this is...

632
00:38:46,220 --> 00:38:47,180
Th-this...

633
00:38:47,180 --> 00:38:49,520
Th-this...

634
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:50,460
Th-this...

635
00:38:50,460 --> 00:38:58,460
Whoa!

636
00:39:09,860 --> 00:39:11,360
What is that?

637
00:39:17,220 --> 00:39:19,200
Aaaaaaah!

638
00:39:19,200 --> 00:39:20,720
Aaaaaaah!

639
00:39:22,220 --> 00:39:24,220
Aaaaaaah!

640
00:39:25,380 --> 00:39:30,360
Aaaaaaah!

641
00:39:32,780 --> 00:39:34,500
Aaaaaaah!

642
00:39:34,500 --> 00:39:38,960
Aaaaaaah!

643
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:41,540
Aaaaaaah!

644
00:39:41,540 --> 00:39:41,780
Aaaaaaah!

645
00:39:41,780 --> 00:39:43,180
Aaaaaaah!

646
00:39:44,220 --> 00:39:45,120
Aaaaaaah!

647
00:40:08,380 --> 00:40:09,960
It might be just you, you know.

648
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:17,260
It's the name Tappei gave to the
remote-controlled UFO he built as a kid.

649
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,080
I don't know.

650
00:40:21,140 --> 00:40:24,940
I have no idea what's
going on with these UFOs.

651
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:28,900
Mommy.

652
00:40:40,080 --> 00:40:43,700
Hey, Mommy, why doesn't Mina have a daddy?

653
00:40:51,220 --> 00:40:52,020
Mina.

654
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:57,520
Daddy rode this and
went far away to the sky.

655
00:40:57,520 --> 00:40:58,520
To the sky.

656
00:40:59,440 --> 00:41:00,220
That's right.

657
00:41:01,260 --> 00:41:07,200
Daddy has been watching over Mina
from far beyond the sky the whole time.

658
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:28,240
This is it.

659
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:31,920
Shocking news has just come in from Japan.

660
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:36,040
An object believed to be a
UFO has appeared over Tokyo.

661
00:41:36,500 --> 00:41:39,800
The UFO that appeared
artificially created a tornado,

662
00:41:39,800 --> 00:41:41,820
destroying a temple in Asakusa,

663
00:41:41,820 --> 00:41:44,560
and then vanished into the sky.

664
00:41:45,100 --> 00:41:46,520
The footage you are watching

665
00:41:46,520 --> 00:41:49,880
was accidentally filmed by a tourist
who happened to be at the scene.

666
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:50,660
It's Hiryumaru.

667
00:41:50,660 --> 00:41:53,080
Mina?

668
00:41:58,440 --> 00:41:59,200
It's going berserk!

669
00:42:01,440 --> 00:42:03,680
Daddy's in Japan.

670
00:42:04,920 --> 00:42:06,220
A UFO, they said?

671
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:11,180
And apparently it appeared over Edogawa,
under Katsushika Police Station's jurisdiction.

672
00:42:12,340 --> 00:42:14,720
Did aliens really invade?

673
00:42:14,720 --> 00:42:16,760
Anyway, we can't just stand here.

674
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:19,280
We have to get back to
Japan as soon as possible.

675
00:42:19,700 --> 00:42:21,980
But we can't just get tickets
on short notice, can we?

676
00:42:22,600 --> 00:42:23,540
Don't worry.

677
00:42:23,540 --> 00:42:25,860
We'll arrange a private plane right away.

678
00:42:26,280 --> 00:42:28,420
Thanks, you'll really do that for me?

679
00:42:28,420 --> 00:42:31,540
I've told you already, I'm innocent!

680
00:42:32,420 --> 00:42:35,740
Without a passport,
I can't even provide identification, can I?

681
00:42:35,740 --> 00:42:39,400
If you'll just let me see Chief Ohara once more,
just once more...

682
00:42:40,320 --> 00:42:43,900
Now that you mention it,
a letter from Mr. Ohara arrived.

683
00:42:43,900 --> 00:42:44,663
The guarantee letter,

684
00:42:44,713 --> 00:42:48,780
So the Chief really was
worried about me after all.

685
00:42:48,780 --> 00:42:49,760
It was over here.

686
00:42:51,060 --> 00:42:51,820
Found it, found it.

687
00:42:53,120 --> 00:42:54,760
Hm? Hm?

688
00:42:57,820 --> 00:43:00,828
Let's make it Danger. That guy's a bad one,

689
00:43:00,878 --> 00:43:03,500
so please make sure he never gets out again.

690
00:43:03,880 --> 00:43:04,440
That's reckless!

691
00:43:06,460 --> 00:43:07,920
Mina's at home?

692
00:43:08,540 --> 00:43:10,877
Y-yeah. Calm down, Lucky.

693
00:43:10,927 --> 00:43:14,287
Mina's Cessna is in the middle
of an overhaul right now.

694
00:43:14,337 --> 00:43:15,360
It can't fly!

695
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:19,580
Don't worry, even Mina wouldn't
pull a stunt like that anymore!

696
00:43:21,840 --> 00:43:22,640
What?!

697
00:43:25,220 --> 00:43:26,880
Are they really holding the trial already?

698
00:43:27,820 --> 00:43:29,000
Sinking the ship is a serious crime,
you know.

699
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:30,280
You'd better be prepared.

700
00:43:30,280 --> 00:43:32,340
Serious, like ten years or so.

701
00:43:32,340 --> 00:43:33,980
Don't be ridiculous.

702
00:43:33,980 --> 00:43:36,700
The laws in Japan and America are different.

703
00:43:37,300 --> 00:43:38,480
Even if you roughly estimate,

704
00:43:38,480 --> 00:43:40,140
it's probably 300 years in prison.

705
00:43:40,860 --> 00:43:41,700
300 years?

706
00:43:42,300 --> 00:43:43,160
This is no joke!

707
00:43:43,160 --> 00:43:45,240
I don't have time for that kind of thing.

708
00:43:45,240 --> 00:43:46,980
Calm down and be quiet.

709
00:43:46,980 --> 00:43:49,820
This isn't a taxi, you know.

710
00:43:50,340 --> 00:43:51,040
Hey!

711
00:43:54,120 --> 00:43:55,060
What is that?

712
00:44:09,880 --> 00:44:10,680
Uncle

713
00:44:11,140 --> 00:44:11,940
What are you doing?

714
00:44:11,940 --> 00:44:12,340
Good.

715
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:15,000
A UFO destroyed the city.

716
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:17,380
Daddy must be in Tokyo too.

717
00:44:17,380 --> 00:44:18,480
It's Tappei!

718
00:44:18,480 --> 00:44:20,140
Alright, let's go together.

719
00:44:20,140 --> 00:44:21,820
Hey, where do you think you're going?

720
00:44:21,820 --> 00:44:22,520
What?

721
00:44:25,080 --> 00:44:25,480
That.

722
00:44:26,780 --> 00:44:27,440
Wait!

723
00:44:27,820 --> 00:44:28,880
Why?!

724
00:44:31,280 --> 00:44:35,140
Hey! You're the one who
said he was the culprit!

725
00:44:35,460 --> 00:44:37,140
Sorry! That was a lie!

726
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:38,340
No way!

727
00:44:40,720 --> 00:44:42,220
No way!

728
00:44:49,940 --> 00:44:52,460
Why is this so embarrassing...

729
00:45:10,420 --> 00:45:10,680
What?

730
00:45:11,840 --> 00:45:12,740
Hey!

731
00:45:14,380 --> 00:45:17,360
Mina, so you really lied to help Tappei!

732
00:45:17,700 --> 00:45:21,120
That's not it!
I just want to hear the truth!

733
00:45:21,640 --> 00:45:23,740
Why did you lie and say he was dead?

734
00:45:24,980 --> 00:45:28,380
Depending on your answer,
I'm going to punch you at least once!

735
00:45:29,000 --> 00:45:30,760
We're going all the way to Japan like this!

736
00:45:31,140 --> 00:45:31,500
What!

737
00:45:31,560 --> 00:45:33,720
What! Wait a minute!
Let's just stop like this!

738
00:45:36,940 --> 00:45:39,920
Sorry, it looks like this
is the only one available.

739
00:45:40,620 --> 00:45:42,400
As expected of Nakagawa's control!

740
00:45:42,400 --> 00:45:44,300
Even a private plane is a jumbo jet?

741
00:45:49,020 --> 00:45:49,980
Yay!

742
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:53,760
I really thought we were done for there.

743
00:45:54,860 --> 00:45:57,340
But you're one hell of a bombshell,
aren't you?

744
00:45:58,000 --> 00:45:59,340
You too, Uncle.

745
00:45:59,340 --> 00:46:01,980
Could you stop calling me "uncle"?

746
00:46:01,980 --> 00:46:04,180
I may not look it, but I'm young.

747
00:46:04,180 --> 00:46:06,420
But you're in the same
class as Daddy, right?

748
00:46:08,560 --> 00:46:10,060
Then what should I call you?

749
00:46:10,760 --> 00:46:13,980
In Kameari, everyone calls me Ryo-san.

750
00:46:13,980 --> 00:46:15,160
Ryo-san

751
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:17,880
What's wrong, Mina?

752
00:46:17,880 --> 00:46:19,220
So, the fuel...

753
00:46:19,220 --> 00:46:23,540
I knew it was impossible to
fly a Zero all the way to Japan.

754
00:46:25,000 --> 00:46:26,680
So what do we do, Ryo-san?

755
00:46:26,680 --> 00:46:27,440
Are we going to die?!

756
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:35,740
We won't last another few minutes.

757
00:46:35,740 --> 00:46:37,320
We're going to fall into the sea!

758
00:46:42,060 --> 00:46:44,180
Alright, I'll handle this somehow.

759
00:46:44,180 --> 00:46:46,320
Ryo-san, what on earth are you going to do?

760
00:46:47,060 --> 00:46:47,780
Anything.

761
00:46:56,340 --> 00:46:57,060
Got it!

762
00:46:58,720 --> 00:46:59,780
W-wow, it's fast!

763
00:46:59,780 --> 00:47:02,120
Of course it is,
they're jet planes after all.

764
00:47:06,780 --> 00:47:10,260
Only four passengers?
It's like a private jet, isn't it?

765
00:47:11,720 --> 00:47:12,460
Still,

766
00:47:12,460 --> 00:47:14,380
I just can't settle down somehow.

767
00:47:15,200 --> 00:47:17,280
I wonder what Ryo-chan is up to right now.

768
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:19,080
By the way,

769
00:47:19,520 --> 00:47:21,980
We ended up leaving him behind in Hawaii,
didn't we?

770
00:47:24,320 --> 00:47:26,420
I'm starting to feel a little sorry for him.

771
00:47:27,480 --> 00:47:30,820
Once we're back in Japan, I suppose
I'll write him up a written apology.

772
00:47:39,380 --> 00:47:41,760
With this,
we'll be towed all the way to Japan!

773
00:47:52,560 --> 00:47:53,140
It's cold.

774
00:47:53,140 --> 00:47:54,980
As expected at 8,000 meters.

775
00:47:55,700 --> 00:47:57,060
Even my body's freezing.

776
00:47:57,060 --> 00:47:59,000
I'm no match for you, Ryo-san.

777
00:48:05,400 --> 00:48:07,220
Finally, my body's thawing out.

778
00:48:07,620 --> 00:48:10,060
Ryo-san, there's a terrible wind here.

779
00:48:12,620 --> 00:48:13,460
It's shaking, isn't it?

780
00:48:13,900 --> 00:48:15,860
Did we get caught in some turbulence,
or did something hit us?

781
00:48:16,300 --> 00:48:19,260
Looks like a large typhoon has formed.

782
00:48:19,260 --> 00:48:20,640
A typhoon

783
00:48:21,040 --> 00:48:22,140
Don't worry.

784
00:48:22,560 --> 00:48:24,260
We won't run into its path.

785
00:48:27,140 --> 00:48:29,820
Ryo-san,
the warning light's about to go out.

786
00:48:42,720 --> 00:48:45,120
This morning,
the day after the astonishing incident,

787
00:48:45,620 --> 00:48:47,960
a countermeasures headquarters has been
set up at Katsushika Police Station.

788
00:48:48,500 --> 00:48:51,980
Wow, I never thought something this
big would happen at our station.

789
00:48:51,980 --> 00:48:53,140
No,

790
00:48:53,860 --> 00:48:57,280
whatever the UFO's true identity,
we will protect the citizens.

791
00:48:57,700 --> 00:48:59,700
That is the mission of the police.

792
00:49:01,320 --> 00:49:04,240
The UFO that flew away suddenly
vanished from radar as well,

793
00:49:04,240 --> 00:49:06,500
and it still hasn't been found.

794
00:49:07,440 --> 00:49:10,700
Now, where shall we blow up next?

795
00:49:13,240 --> 00:49:14,220
That's enough, don't you think?

796
00:49:14,920 --> 00:49:17,720
Destroying that much should have
been a sufficient demonstration.

797
00:49:18,800 --> 00:49:20,200
Not nearly enough.

798
00:49:20,680 --> 00:49:24,580
We need to show them even
more of Hiryumaru's terror.

799
00:49:27,020 --> 00:49:27,600
I refuse!

800
00:49:28,040 --> 00:49:30,100
How can you keep doing
such a terrible thing?

801
00:49:37,360 --> 00:49:40,960
You're the one who built that terrible weapon,
you know.

802
00:49:41,420 --> 00:49:42,820
No, Hiryumaru is -

803
00:49:43,520 --> 00:49:44,440
It is not!

804
00:49:44,440 --> 00:49:48,400
You're our accomplice now.

805
00:49:48,880 --> 00:49:51,020
Don't you ever think about
going against us again.

806
00:49:54,780 --> 00:49:56,840
Look, I can see Japan!

807
00:50:13,260 --> 00:50:14,140
Come on, Konji!

808
00:50:14,140 --> 00:50:16,820
Let's make our company trip to Hawaii too.

809
00:50:18,220 --> 00:50:21,080
If we go to Hawaii,
we'll get to meet Agnes Lum, right?

810
00:50:21,080 --> 00:50:22,140
We might, but...

811
00:50:22,480 --> 00:50:25,700
That Weekly Playboy is from Showa 50,
you know.

812
00:50:44,480 --> 00:50:45,720
What's going on?

813
00:50:51,000 --> 00:50:52,880
It's Agnes Lum!

814
00:50:56,760 --> 00:50:57,360
Yes!

815
00:50:57,360 --> 00:51:00,240
Now then, Gonji, Volvo,
thanks for holding down the fort.

816
00:51:01,980 --> 00:51:03,400
What are you doing, Volvo?

817
00:51:03,400 --> 00:51:07,120
Ryotsu, that's one huge Hawaiian souvenir.

818
00:51:07,520 --> 00:51:09,300
Like hell this is a souvenir!

819
00:51:21,500 --> 00:51:22,140
What's that?

820
00:51:22,280 --> 00:51:23,300
It's the Hiryūbaru.

821
00:51:23,300 --> 00:51:24,560
Let's go, Ryo-san.

822
00:51:25,120 --> 00:51:25,840
Here we go.

823
00:51:33,340 --> 00:51:35,360
General, I'm back.

824
00:51:36,320 --> 00:51:37,820
Ohara.

825
00:51:38,380 --> 00:51:41,120
This is the biggest incident in Katsushika station's history,
isn't it?

826
00:51:41,640 --> 00:51:45,600
We eagerly set up a task force,
but

827
00:51:45,600 --> 00:51:48,740
that a UFO attack isn't part
of our first-response duties,

828
00:51:48,740 --> 00:51:51,100
and it was transferred to headquarters.

829
00:51:52,000 --> 00:51:55,040
So, it really is an alien invasion?

830
00:51:55,480 --> 00:51:56,480
No way!

831
00:51:56,980 --> 00:51:58,520
Chief, what's the situation?

832
00:51:58,940 --> 00:52:01,460
We still haven't got the slightest idea.

833
00:52:24,200 --> 00:52:27,800
Landing right at a police station? How bold!

834
00:52:27,800 --> 00:52:31,940
Could it be an alien invasion after all,
like Terai said?

835
00:52:32,500 --> 00:52:33,940
Guess we'll just have to ask them.

836
00:52:34,360 --> 00:52:36,060
Someone, bring the loudspeaker!

837
00:52:36,060 --> 00:52:40,280
Ahhh! Who are you people?

838
00:52:40,280 --> 00:52:42,080
Which planet did you come from?

839
00:52:47,800 --> 00:52:49,300
No response

840
00:52:49,820 --> 00:52:52,800
Maybe our language just doesn't
get through to them, right?

841
00:52:52,800 --> 00:52:54,980
Then what are we supposed to do?

842
00:52:54,980 --> 00:52:55,340
Right.

843
00:53:01,880 --> 00:53:04,200
That thing isn't a UFO at all.

844
00:53:04,720 --> 00:53:05,480
Ryo-chan.

845
00:53:05,480 --> 00:53:06,260
Senpai.

846
00:53:06,260 --> 00:53:07,440
That girl is...

847
00:53:09,300 --> 00:53:10,180
Papa.

848
00:53:10,180 --> 00:53:11,160
Everyone, wait!

849
00:53:11,160 --> 00:53:13,920
Let go, Ryo-san, let go!

850
00:53:13,920 --> 00:53:16,740
How did you get back from Hawaii?

851
00:53:17,240 --> 00:53:19,860
Never mind that. That thing isn't a UFO,

852
00:53:19,860 --> 00:53:21,880
it's the Hiryumaru that Tappei built.

853
00:53:22,420 --> 00:53:25,660
Hiryumaru? Who's this Tappei?

854
00:53:25,660 --> 00:53:28,700
My father was kidnapped in Hawaii.

855
00:53:28,700 --> 00:53:30,800
Gentlemen of the Japanese police.

856
00:53:30,800 --> 00:53:31,780
It talked!

857
00:53:32,420 --> 00:53:34,180
Still, we're being treated with contempt.

858
00:53:34,600 --> 00:53:37,800
A pathetic police station
like this as our headquarters?

859
00:53:38,860 --> 00:53:40,880
Then just take it to headquarters.

860
00:53:40,880 --> 00:53:41,640
Let me borrow that for a sec.

861
00:53:42,420 --> 00:53:44,620
Hey, who the hell are you?

862
00:53:44,620 --> 00:53:49,080
Ugh, you can just call me Tiger.

863
00:53:49,640 --> 00:53:54,180
It's Tiger! What's wrong with it?
I'm not showing off.

864
00:53:55,000 --> 00:54:04,220
What's your goal, anyway? What the hell is this?
We demand 10 billion yen from the Japanese government.

865
00:54:05,140 --> 00:54:06,500
10 billion yen.

866
00:54:06,500 --> 00:54:09,180
Have it ready within 24 hours.

867
00:54:09,740 --> 00:54:13,500
Or else the capital,
Tokyo, will be destroyed.

868
00:54:14,020 --> 00:54:14,680
Do it.

869
00:54:17,420 --> 00:54:18,800
Watch closely.

870
00:54:18,800 --> 00:54:20,460
This devilish weapon.

871
00:54:20,460 --> 00:54:22,320
It's the terror of the Hiryumaru.

872
00:54:24,080 --> 00:54:24,920
Papa.

873
00:54:24,920 --> 00:54:26,700
Wait, everyone, it's dangerous!

874
00:54:46,860 --> 00:54:48,200
We have no choice but to win, mmph!

875
00:55:16,140 --> 00:55:16,880
Damn it!

876
00:55:18,720 --> 00:55:22,100
The disc-shaped weapon that
destroyed Sensō-ji yesterday

877
00:55:22,100 --> 00:55:25,520
has been identified as belonging to
a terrorist group calling itself Tiger.

878
00:55:26,220 --> 00:55:29,780
Tiger is demanding 10 billion
yen from the Japanese government.

879
00:55:30,200 --> 00:55:34,500
They've issued a statement that if this is not complied with,
they will destroy Tokyo.

880
00:55:35,420 --> 00:55:37,960
The government has immediately
begun discussions on a response.

881
00:55:41,580 --> 00:55:45,140
So the people who sank the
ship in Hawaii are the culprits?

882
00:55:45,480 --> 00:55:46,680
There's no doubt about it.

883
00:55:48,200 --> 00:55:48,660
Inside that...

884
00:55:48,660 --> 00:55:49,104
Chief,

885
00:55:49,154 --> 00:55:52,780
Isn't there some way to rescue Tappei?

886
00:55:53,400 --> 00:55:55,740
But when it comes to dealing
with the Japanese government...

887
00:55:55,740 --> 00:55:57,920
Ah, Chief!

888
00:55:58,960 --> 00:56:02,880
It looks like the government has
decided to reject Tiger's demands.

889
00:56:02,880 --> 00:56:03,540
What?

890
00:56:04,180 --> 00:56:07,020
But Tappei is trapped inside that thing!

891
00:56:07,640 --> 00:56:08,520
It can't be helped.

892
00:56:08,520 --> 00:56:12,300
The government's policy is
never to give in to terrorism.

893
00:56:12,300 --> 00:56:12,940
No way.

894
00:56:16,020 --> 00:56:16,800
What's that?

895
00:56:19,320 --> 00:56:21,640
Surely it's not a plane about
to be shot down by missiles?

896
00:56:23,040 --> 00:56:24,740
Don't worry, that's a reconnaissance plane.

897
00:56:25,340 --> 00:56:26,420
Everyone, come here!

898
00:56:26,880 --> 00:56:28,620
Hey, Ryotsu, where are you going?

899
00:56:35,220 --> 00:56:37,920
Boss, a jet is approaching!

900
00:56:38,400 --> 00:56:40,460
It looks like a Self-Defense
Forces reconnaissance plane.

901
00:56:40,960 --> 00:56:44,680
Looks like they still don't understand
how terrifying this Hiryumaru is.

902
00:56:45,280 --> 00:56:46,600
Bring it down with a tornado!

903
00:57:01,860 --> 00:57:03,880
This is what happens when you mess with me!

904
00:57:03,880 --> 00:57:07,100
If it comes to this, I'll smash
everything even more spectacularly.

905
00:57:08,960 --> 00:57:09,360
Right.

906
00:57:11,080 --> 00:57:11,820
Yes!

907
00:57:12,820 --> 00:57:13,360
Ready... go!

908
00:57:14,540 --> 00:57:15,160
Hey!

909
00:57:15,160 --> 00:57:16,360
Alright, Kankichi!

910
00:57:18,200 --> 00:57:18,860
What are you doing?!

911
00:57:19,580 --> 00:57:21,800
The Zero's out of fuel, so!

912
00:57:24,460 --> 00:57:25,640
It's fine, we can still fly!

913
00:57:26,740 --> 00:57:28,300
Right! Barbo, Sagonji!

914
00:57:28,560 --> 00:57:29,040
Alright!

915
00:57:30,840 --> 00:57:34,260
What do you plan to do
flying a big plane like this?

916
00:57:34,460 --> 00:57:35,980
We're up against a UFO!

917
00:57:36,800 --> 00:57:39,820
You can't let yourself be
egged on by this caveman!

918
00:57:40,520 --> 00:57:42,160
I want to save my dad!

919
00:57:42,460 --> 00:57:45,320
You don't know everyone's
piloting techniques!

920
00:57:45,500 --> 00:57:47,220
Alright! Everyone, let's go!

921
00:57:50,480 --> 00:57:52,240
Whoa, that's dangerous!

922
00:57:59,040 --> 00:58:01,320
What, now the Hiryumaru is
going for the one on top...

923
00:58:23,400 --> 00:58:24,720
Make it flashier.

924
00:58:24,720 --> 00:58:27,140
I hate Tokyo.

925
00:58:28,000 --> 00:58:30,840
Blow up Asakusa, Ueno, everything.

926
00:58:31,640 --> 00:58:32,380
Why?

927
00:58:32,380 --> 00:58:34,160
You, who was born in America,

928
00:58:34,160 --> 00:58:36,140
why do you hate Tokyo so much?

929
00:58:36,140 --> 00:58:36,860
Shut up.

930
00:58:37,380 --> 00:58:38,760
I just hate it, that's all.

931
00:58:39,240 --> 00:58:41,060
Boss, something's approaching.

932
00:58:41,980 --> 00:58:43,440
What, another jet?

933
00:58:43,440 --> 00:58:46,800
No, it seems smaller and slower.

934
00:58:53,840 --> 00:58:55,480
What? Isn't that a Zero?

935
00:58:56,140 --> 00:58:57,140
Are you mocking us?

936
00:58:58,420 --> 00:59:00,120
Yeah, I'll blow it away with a tornado!

937
00:59:12,620 --> 00:59:14,800
Damn that smug bastard.

938
00:59:15,220 --> 00:59:18,120
Got it, up! Fly higher than the Hiryumaru!

939
00:59:18,840 --> 00:59:19,400
I know!

940
00:59:26,940 --> 00:59:27,940
No way I'm letting that happen.

941
00:59:45,580 --> 00:59:47,900
Forget it, we can't get any closer at all.

942
00:59:47,900 --> 00:59:48,740
Damn it!

943
00:59:50,000 --> 00:59:50,720
The fuel...

944
00:59:50,720 --> 00:59:53,400
As I thought,
the enemy patrol car isn't nearly enough.

945
00:59:54,000 --> 00:59:56,140
Alright!
If it comes to this, it's do or die!

946
00:59:56,500 --> 00:59:58,440
Get under the tornado once!

947
01:00:03,540 --> 01:00:04,320
Where?

948
01:00:04,540 --> 01:00:05,740
Looks like it's entered Shikoku!

949
01:00:12,180 --> 01:00:12,720
There it is!

950
01:00:15,660 --> 01:00:16,240
It's above!

951
01:00:16,660 --> 01:00:17,380
What!?

952
01:00:18,860 --> 01:00:20,500
Alright! Leave the rest to me!

953
01:00:22,040 --> 01:00:22,880
Ryo-kun!

954
01:00:23,500 --> 01:00:24,280
Go ahead!

955
01:00:24,480 --> 01:00:25,800
Yaah!

956
01:00:25,800 --> 01:00:27,600
Kojieda!

957
01:00:27,900 --> 01:00:28,300
Yaah!

958
01:00:28,560 --> 01:00:30,860
Ugh, ugh, ugh, yaah!

959
01:00:32,060 --> 01:00:32,840
That's...

960
01:00:33,540 --> 01:00:34,300
Mina!

961
01:00:35,020 --> 01:00:35,860
Mina?

962
01:00:36,240 --> 01:00:37,180
Who's that?

963
01:00:37,540 --> 01:00:38,540
She's my daughter!

964
01:00:39,080 --> 01:00:39,520
Daughter?

965
01:00:40,400 --> 01:00:42,300
S-someone's on top of the aircraft!

966
01:00:42,820 --> 01:00:43,540
What?

967
01:00:43,740 --> 01:00:44,580
Hah!

968
01:00:44,600 --> 01:00:45,560
Shake her off!

969
01:00:50,320 --> 01:00:51,100
Mina!

970
01:00:53,500 --> 01:00:54,720
Aaaaaah!

971
01:00:59,420 --> 01:01:02,640
Everyone, hurry! The power's running out!

972
01:01:03,080 --> 01:01:03,700
Got it!

973
01:01:07,500 --> 01:01:08,040
Everyone!

974
01:01:09,120 --> 01:01:12,600
Who said you could stop
the tornado on your own!

975
01:01:13,780 --> 01:01:14,240
Sappe!

976
01:01:15,320 --> 01:01:17,100
We're the Ryotsu Ship Knights!

977
01:01:17,540 --> 01:01:18,880
Stop the Hiryumaru!

978
01:01:19,560 --> 01:01:20,220
Ship Knights?

979
01:01:20,700 --> 01:01:21,680
What is this guy!

980
01:01:52,540 --> 01:01:53,480
It's terrible!

981
01:01:53,480 --> 01:01:56,480
I heard the Hiryumaru
crashed onto Nakagawa Bridge.

982
01:01:56,480 --> 01:01:56,900
What?

983
01:01:56,900 --> 01:01:59,040
It must be Ryo-chan and
the others who did it.

984
01:01:59,500 --> 01:02:01,060
Quickly, arrest Tiger.

985
01:02:01,520 --> 01:02:04,300
But I think we shouldn't
move at the initial stage,

986
01:02:07,300 --> 01:02:09,040
isn't this under our jurisdiction?

987
01:02:11,780 --> 01:02:12,520
Tappei!

988
01:02:34,540 --> 01:02:36,420
Why is everyone here in Japan?

989
01:02:37,040 --> 01:02:38,200
Isn't it obvious?

990
01:02:38,200 --> 01:02:39,860
We came to rescue you.

991
01:02:43,680 --> 01:02:44,620
Ryotsu!

992
01:02:45,080 --> 01:02:46,080
We've come to save you!

993
01:02:58,100 --> 01:02:58,720
Get out of the way!

994
01:03:00,680 --> 01:03:01,640
Where's Tiger?

995
01:03:01,640 --> 01:03:02,960
He's still inside.

996
01:03:03,280 --> 01:03:04,800
Right, charge in!

997
01:03:04,940 --> 01:03:05,640
Argh!

998
01:03:06,780 --> 01:03:08,240
Go, go, go!

999
01:03:08,240 --> 01:03:08,940
Look out!

1000
01:03:22,780 --> 01:03:23,600
Damn it!

1001
01:03:29,460 --> 01:03:30,200
Kankichi.

1002
01:03:30,960 --> 01:03:33,920
Ever since we were kids,
you've always been there to save me.

1003
01:03:34,920 --> 01:03:35,920
That's not true.

1004
01:03:35,920 --> 01:03:38,820
It's me who should thank you.

1005
01:03:39,220 --> 01:03:41,180
You call that saving someone?

1006
01:03:43,340 --> 01:03:46,120
Remember? The spring break in third year?

1007
01:03:46,120 --> 01:03:50,340
When the kid boss from another
school was picking on me.

1008
01:03:54,300 --> 01:03:56,320
I'll take this one.

1009
01:03:56,320 --> 01:03:59,560
Stop it! Give it back! I said give it back!

1010
01:04:00,140 --> 01:04:07,860
Hey! What's wrong, crybaby?
If you want it back, come and get it.

1011
01:04:08,660 --> 01:04:09,220
Wait!

1012
01:04:11,700 --> 01:04:14,760
You bastard! What the hell do you
think you're doing to my friend?

1013
01:04:15,540 --> 01:04:16,640
Don-kichi...

1014
01:04:17,440 --> 01:04:20,280
You want a piece of me?

1015
01:04:30,120 --> 01:04:31,260
There you go!

1016
01:04:36,580 --> 01:04:38,580
I've forgotten all about that.

1017
01:04:39,840 --> 01:04:41,800
I remember it well.

1018
01:04:43,060 --> 01:04:45,120
Damn it, you'd better remember this.

1019
01:04:46,980 --> 01:04:48,680
It was like when Earth was in danger,

1020
01:04:48,680 --> 01:04:51,220
you were like a hero
who came from outer space.

1021
01:04:54,660 --> 01:04:57,220
I wanted to be like Kankichi too,

1022
01:04:58,200 --> 01:04:59,480
but I never could.

1023
01:05:01,260 --> 01:05:01,660
Or rather, I...

1024
01:05:03,140 --> 01:05:04,220
Tappei...

1025
01:05:04,220 --> 01:05:10,340
Tappei, I know.

1026
01:05:26,200 --> 01:05:26,840
I... I...

1027
01:05:33,780 --> 01:05:34,420
Papa

1028
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:38,640
I'm sorry.

1029
01:05:43,340 --> 01:05:45,060
I'm really sorry.

1030
01:05:45,480 --> 01:05:47,280
I couldn't do anything for you until now.

1031
01:05:47,280 --> 01:05:48,220
Papa

1032
01:05:48,220 --> 01:05:49,360
I'm sorry.

1033
01:05:51,040 --> 01:05:53,140
It's all my fault.

1034
01:05:53,660 --> 01:05:54,340
Sor -

1035
01:05:54,340 --> 01:05:57,720
Sorry, sorry, sorry...

1036
01:05:57,720 --> 01:06:00,620
Is that really what you say to your daughter,
the first time you've met her?

1037
01:06:01,640 --> 01:06:02,300
Hey.

1038
01:06:02,300 --> 01:06:05,520
That's not the words I wanted to hear.

1039
01:06:06,220 --> 01:06:07,320
Everyone.

1040
01:06:07,320 --> 01:06:08,260
Wait a moment!

1041
01:06:13,740 --> 01:06:14,480
Tappei

1042
01:06:25,460 --> 01:06:26,900
Don't worry.

1043
01:06:26,900 --> 01:06:28,640
Those guys are with me.

1044
01:06:37,620 --> 01:06:40,440
Tappei, what on earth happened?

1045
01:06:40,800 --> 01:06:42,060
Won't you tell me?

1046
01:06:44,100 --> 01:06:47,100
I was deceived for a long time.

1047
01:06:48,200 --> 01:06:50,020
In the letters to Cathy
that never got a reply,

1048
01:06:50,620 --> 01:06:53,700
I thought I'd been abandoned,
the research fool that I am.

1049
01:06:54,540 --> 01:06:56,480
Of course, I didn't know about Mina either.

1050
01:06:57,160 --> 01:07:00,980
But that was all a scheme by
Tiger to keep me from going back.

1051
01:07:01,960 --> 01:07:05,360
So that's why I was made to
research that terrifying weapon.

1052
01:07:06,380 --> 01:07:08,460
The Hiryumaru isn't a weapon at all.

1053
01:07:09,200 --> 01:07:13,240
What I was researching was a
machine to wipe out typhoons.

1054
01:07:13,980 --> 01:07:15,860
Wipe out typhoons.

1055
01:07:21,220 --> 01:07:24,580
Can they really erase a typhoon?

1056
01:07:25,440 --> 01:07:29,640
Yes. The Hiryumaru super-compresses the
plasma-decomposed atmosphere and stores it,

1057
01:07:31,260 --> 01:07:34,246
then releases it explosively
as a reduction at the center,

1058
01:07:34,296 --> 01:07:36,900
and that's how it can wipe out a typhoon.

1059
01:07:37,780 --> 01:07:40,860
Even with that explanation,
I don't understand a thing.

1060
01:07:41,120 --> 01:07:44,240
Won't Tiger use the
Hiryumaru to attack us again?

1061
01:07:45,040 --> 01:07:46,260
There's no need to worry about that.

1062
01:07:46,700 --> 01:07:48,574
Tiger may be able to pilot it,

1063
01:07:48,624 --> 01:07:51,140
but he can't create a tornado.

1064
01:07:58,100 --> 01:07:59,020
Hey, Naoko.

1065
01:07:59,820 --> 01:08:02,660
Aren't you hungry?
Let's go get something to eat.

1066
01:08:02,660 --> 01:08:05,260
Yeah, but what about Mina?

1067
01:08:05,260 --> 01:08:08,460
Wouldn't Mina perk up too if
she ate something delicious?

1068
01:08:08,820 --> 01:08:10,940
True. So what should we get?

1069
01:08:19,240 --> 01:08:20,740
Right, then it's settled.

1070
01:08:21,140 --> 01:08:21,220
Yeah.

1071
01:08:21,760 --> 01:08:22,480
Mina.

1072
01:08:24,520 --> 01:08:25,320
Mina?

1073
01:08:25,800 --> 01:08:26,600
Mina?

1074
01:08:26,960 --> 01:08:27,920
Mina!

1075
01:08:34,580 --> 01:08:36,040
Yes, Katsushika Station.

1076
01:08:36,440 --> 01:08:36,980
It's me.

1077
01:08:37,580 --> 01:08:38,760
That voice is Tiger!

1078
01:08:39,120 --> 01:08:39,560
What?

1079
01:08:41,540 --> 01:08:43,260
We have Mina.

1080
01:08:43,260 --> 01:08:46,640
If you want her back safe, bring Tappei.

1081
01:08:46,640 --> 01:08:47,240
What?

1082
01:08:47,560 --> 01:08:48,160
Damn it!

1083
01:08:48,160 --> 01:08:53,680
At six tomorrow morning, come by boat to Daiba No.
6 from Shinagawa Outer Harbor.

1084
01:08:54,360 --> 01:08:57,360
Don't be ridiculous.
Making demands like that is outrageous.

1085
01:08:59,820 --> 01:09:11,640
Here it comes... you'd go this far? Please, let me go in his place. Tappei, no way!
If you fall into Tiger's hands, he'll whip up another tornado and the town will - no!

1086
01:09:11,640 --> 01:09:14,860
I won't let that happen again. Please.

1087
01:09:24,660 --> 01:09:28,260
I'm gonna crush Tokyo soon, you know.

1088
01:09:28,260 --> 01:09:31,660
What's with the manga-villain talk?

1089
01:09:31,660 --> 01:09:35,260
Anyway, your goal is money, right?

1090
01:09:35,260 --> 01:09:36,680
Lame.

1091
01:09:36,680 --> 01:09:39,800
Hey, how dare you talk
to the boss like that!

1092
01:09:40,180 --> 01:09:42,180
I'm calling it lame because it is lame.

1093
01:09:42,700 --> 01:09:43,980
Ugh, how uncool.

1094
01:09:44,520 --> 01:09:47,360
Anyway, what do you even hope
to gain by destroying Tokyo?

1095
01:09:49,140 --> 01:09:49,940
Revenge.

1096
01:09:50,520 --> 01:09:51,240
Revenge?

1097
01:09:51,780 --> 01:09:55,320
When I was a kid,
I lived in this town for one year.

1098
01:09:55,880 --> 01:09:59,760
During that time, I suffered the
one humiliating incident of my life.

1099
01:10:00,560 --> 01:10:02,140
A humiliating incident?

1100
01:10:02,760 --> 01:10:04,320
I swore to myself

1101
01:10:04,840 --> 01:10:07,040
that someday I'd get revenge on this town.

1102
01:10:07,040 --> 01:10:09,420
I'd crush this town, that's what I decided.

1103
01:10:09,420 --> 01:10:11,020
How stupid.

1104
01:10:11,020 --> 01:10:11,580
What?

1105
01:10:12,040 --> 01:10:15,140
You said revenge,
so I thought it'd be something big,

1106
01:10:15,140 --> 01:10:18,220
but it's just a childhood grudge, isn't it?

1107
01:10:18,940 --> 01:10:19,500
Shut up.

1108
01:10:20,700 --> 01:10:21,680
Don't you forget it.

1109
01:10:21,680 --> 01:10:23,840
You're a hostage, you know.

1110
01:10:24,540 --> 01:10:25,420
Sorry, but

1111
01:10:25,820 --> 01:10:28,180
holding me hostage won't mean much.

1112
01:10:28,780 --> 01:10:29,140
What?

1113
01:10:30,700 --> 01:10:32,600
Are you saying I'm worthless?

1114
01:10:33,840 --> 01:10:34,820
That's not true.

1115
01:10:34,820 --> 01:10:37,780
Tappei will definitely come to save you.

1116
01:10:37,780 --> 01:10:38,900
No way that's happening.

1117
01:10:40,320 --> 01:10:43,140
He's always been worried about his family.

1118
01:10:45,140 --> 01:10:48,280
He must have gone back to Hawaii for good.

1119
01:10:49,760 --> 01:10:52,020
I threw away all the letters from Hawaii.

1120
01:10:52,620 --> 01:10:54,840
Even the letter saying a
daughter had been born came,

1121
01:10:55,380 --> 01:10:58,880
so I replied that Tappei
had died in an accident.

1122
01:11:04,680 --> 01:11:07,200
That's awful! You're the lowest of the low!

1123
01:11:08,440 --> 01:11:09,640
Say whatever you want.

1124
01:11:09,640 --> 01:11:11,640
Anyway, he's coming.

1125
01:11:12,100 --> 01:11:12,900
Absolutely.

1126
01:11:20,500 --> 01:11:23,240
You came up with a decoy plan, didn't you.

1127
01:11:24,060 --> 01:11:27,720
We can't hand Tappei over to Tiger,
no matter what.

1128
01:11:27,720 --> 01:11:30,460
But what if they figure out it's a fake?

1129
01:11:30,880 --> 01:11:31,600
Don't worry.

1130
01:11:31,600 --> 01:11:33,820
Honda's build is a close match too.

1131
01:11:33,820 --> 01:11:36,740
As long as nobody catches on until the hostage exchange,
we're fine.

1132
01:11:37,760 --> 01:11:40,080
First, we need to rescue Mina.

1133
01:11:41,220 --> 01:11:43,560
Even so,
Honda really does look just like him.

1134
01:11:44,680 --> 01:11:47,120
From a distance, he's Tappei himself.

1135
01:11:47,900 --> 01:11:49,780
How about it? Pretty convincing, right?

1136
01:11:51,020 --> 01:11:53,080
H-hey, what are you doing?

1137
01:11:54,720 --> 01:11:56,160
Then who's this Tappei?

1138
01:11:56,280 --> 01:11:58,400
That's the real Tappei-san!

1139
01:11:59,020 --> 01:12:01,160
Senpai, since when?

1140
01:12:01,280 --> 01:12:04,100
Ryo-chan, you were planning this all along,
weren't you?

1141
01:12:04,440 --> 01:12:05,040
Mmmm!

1142
01:12:05,160 --> 01:12:07,660
Ryotsu, Ryotsu, answer me, Ryotsu!

1143
01:12:08,160 --> 01:12:09,380
Sorry, Chief!

1144
01:12:09,780 --> 01:12:12,320
I really want to let
Tappei go no matter what!

1145
01:12:12,600 --> 01:12:13,020
But!

1146
01:12:13,280 --> 01:12:15,440
Anyway, leave it to me!

1147
01:12:20,700 --> 01:12:22,200
Don't worry, Tappei.

1148
01:12:22,580 --> 01:12:24,300
We'll rescue Mina safely.

1149
01:12:24,300 --> 01:12:27,100
I won't hand you over to Tiger either.

1150
01:12:27,720 --> 01:12:28,340
Kankichi

1151
01:12:46,320 --> 01:12:47,160
Tiger

1152
01:12:47,520 --> 01:12:48,460
Where's Mina?

1153
01:12:49,320 --> 01:12:51,600
Unfortunately, she's not here.

1154
01:12:52,020 --> 01:12:52,360
What?

1155
01:12:53,420 --> 01:12:54,440
Look behind you.

1156
01:12:56,320 --> 01:12:58,320
My daughter is over there.

1157
01:13:00,980 --> 01:13:02,100
Mina, you...

1158
01:13:02,100 --> 01:13:04,960
Mina is inside the Yurikamome.

1159
01:13:04,960 --> 01:13:07,240
I'll contact the new
transit system right away.

1160
01:13:08,320 --> 01:13:10,900
Tappei, come over here quietly.

1161
01:13:11,600 --> 01:13:14,240
Damn, if Mina's stuck
in a place like that...

1162
01:13:14,900 --> 01:13:17,840
Hurry up, or do you not care
what happens to your daughter?

1163
01:13:19,080 --> 01:13:19,680
Tappei

1164
01:13:20,280 --> 01:13:22,420
There's no other way to save Mina.

1165
01:13:23,040 --> 01:13:24,320
I'm her father.

1166
01:13:24,940 --> 01:13:25,780
Tappei

1167
01:13:31,000 --> 01:13:33,140
The Yurikamome's system has been destroyed.

1168
01:13:33,140 --> 01:13:33,360
What?

1169
01:13:33,960 --> 01:13:35,340
This must be Haigan's doing.

1170
01:13:35,340 --> 01:13:36,100
Damn it!

1171
01:13:37,280 --> 01:13:39,060
Borubōsa Konji, do you read me?

1172
01:13:39,060 --> 01:13:40,780
Heading for the Yurikamome.

1173
01:13:41,100 --> 01:13:41,720
One.

1174
01:13:46,340 --> 01:13:48,560
Tappei is going into the Hiryumaru!

1175
01:13:50,360 --> 01:13:52,040
There, that should be enough.

1176
01:13:52,600 --> 01:13:54,340
Hurry up and release Mina!

1177
01:13:54,940 --> 01:13:55,600
No way.

1178
01:13:55,600 --> 01:13:56,000
What?

1179
01:13:57,200 --> 01:13:58,600
First, create a tornado.

1180
01:13:58,600 --> 01:14:01,340
Otherwise, I won't release the daughter.

1181
01:14:01,340 --> 01:14:02,460
Ugh... damn it.

1182
01:14:06,580 --> 01:14:07,520
Tappei.

1183
01:14:18,960 --> 01:14:19,320
What?

1184
01:14:20,960 --> 01:14:21,780
What did you do?

1185
01:14:21,780 --> 01:14:24,600
If it keeps taking in air like this,

1186
01:14:24,980 --> 01:14:27,120
the internal pressure will
reach its limit in 30 minutes.

1187
01:14:28,120 --> 01:14:29,740
The Hiryumaru will self-destruct.

1188
01:14:30,380 --> 01:14:30,740
What?

1189
01:14:31,640 --> 01:14:33,480
Now, release Mina!

1190
01:14:34,120 --> 01:14:36,100
The Hiryumaru has started moving!

1191
01:14:36,640 --> 01:14:38,840
Don't tell me Tappei is making a tornado...

1192
01:14:39,360 --> 01:14:39,720
No way...

1193
01:14:41,720 --> 01:14:41,820
This way!

1194
01:14:42,000 --> 01:14:42,500
Roger!

1195
01:14:42,820 --> 01:14:44,520
Going in!

1196
01:14:46,940 --> 01:14:48,700
Idiot! It's too early!

1197
01:14:50,820 --> 01:14:51,700
Police!

1198
01:14:51,880 --> 01:14:52,580
Move!

1199
01:14:53,300 --> 01:14:54,080
Y-yes!

1200
01:14:56,480 --> 01:14:57,220
Damn it!

1201
01:15:03,300 --> 01:15:06,120
The Hiryumaru won't go
the way you want anymore!

1202
01:15:06,360 --> 01:15:08,240
Come on, let Mina go!

1203
01:15:10,400 --> 01:15:11,200
Damn you!

1204
01:15:14,700 --> 01:15:17,960
Tappei!

1205
01:15:17,960 --> 01:15:18,860
No!

1206
01:15:18,860 --> 01:15:20,720
The Hiryumaru has started moving.

1207
01:15:20,720 --> 01:15:22,840
Leave the rest to me.

1208
01:15:22,840 --> 01:15:23,680
No way!

1209
01:15:23,680 --> 01:15:26,360
It'll self-destruct 30
minutes after Giriuma.

1210
01:15:26,360 --> 01:15:27,120
What?

1211
01:15:27,120 --> 01:15:30,180
He had no choice, that's what happened.

1212
01:15:30,180 --> 01:15:31,680
I'll handle this part.

1213
01:15:31,680 --> 01:15:32,900
You can't be seen.

1214
01:15:32,900 --> 01:15:34,220
But...

1215
01:15:34,220 --> 01:15:36,320
You're his father, aren't you?

1216
01:15:36,320 --> 01:15:37,620
Hurry up and go!

1217
01:16:20,380 --> 01:16:20,940
No way.

1218
01:16:26,380 --> 01:16:28,280
Mist swirls, a tornado rises!

1219
01:16:28,280 --> 01:16:29,320
This is bad!

1220
01:16:30,140 --> 01:16:30,920
Yes, yes.

1221
01:16:31,520 --> 01:16:32,080
Yes.

1222
01:16:33,920 --> 01:16:35,900
Chief, you have a call.

1223
01:16:35,900 --> 01:16:38,580
What is it at a time like this?

1224
01:16:38,580 --> 01:16:39,280
Well, it's...

1225
01:16:40,460 --> 01:16:41,740
It took off, but...

1226
01:16:41,740 --> 01:16:43,440
Th-that's...

1227
01:16:43,440 --> 01:16:44,920
Did it take off?

1228
01:16:44,920 --> 01:16:47,420
What on earth is going on here?

1229
01:16:47,420 --> 01:16:49,220
W-well, you see...

1230
01:16:58,780 --> 01:17:00,260
This hijacking is a disaster!

1231
01:17:00,980 --> 01:17:01,340
Do it!

1232
01:17:12,240 --> 01:17:13,180
He actually went and did it!

1233
01:17:14,420 --> 01:17:15,660
What have you done!

1234
01:17:25,740 --> 01:17:26,460
The Unicorn!

1235
01:17:30,900 --> 01:17:33,340
So that's how he lost to a Japanese cop.

1236
01:17:33,340 --> 01:17:36,340
Come on, you're hurting me.

1237
01:17:36,340 --> 01:17:37,660
It hurts.

1238
01:17:37,660 --> 01:17:40,200
Die.

1239
01:17:45,880 --> 01:17:46,920
Die.

1240
01:17:59,460 --> 01:18:24,960
!

1241
01:18:24,960 --> 01:18:26,480
W-w-w-well, you see, this is...!

1242
01:18:28,820 --> 01:18:31,500
If this goes on,
the Yurikamome will fall into the sea!

1243
01:18:37,800 --> 01:18:38,440
A tornado!

1244
01:18:56,960 --> 01:18:58,280
I'll take my guest...

1245
01:18:59,300 --> 01:19:00,500
Mina!

1246
01:19:02,000 --> 01:19:02,580
Daddy!

1247
01:19:03,960 --> 01:19:04,780
Daddy, I...

1248
01:19:05,420 --> 01:19:07,620
Talk later. Get out of here quickly!

1249
01:19:13,000 --> 01:19:15,260
It's no good! They won't let us get close!

1250
01:19:15,620 --> 01:19:19,160
We only have a brief window to save
her before it falls off the bridge!

1251
01:19:23,460 --> 01:19:23,900
Now!

1252
01:19:25,460 --> 01:19:27,080
Hurry!

1253
01:19:27,080 --> 01:19:28,420
Yes.

1254
01:19:35,440 --> 01:19:37,300
Mama

1255
01:19:53,900 --> 01:19:54,240
Whoa!

1256
01:19:54,900 --> 01:19:56,620
Nooo!

1257
01:20:02,660 --> 01:20:04,540
Nooo!

1258
01:20:04,540 --> 01:20:06,340
Nooo!

1259
01:20:06,340 --> 01:20:07,440
Nooo!

1260
01:20:07,440 --> 01:20:08,740
Nooo!

1261
01:20:08,740 --> 01:20:09,860
Nooo!

1262
01:20:09,860 --> 01:20:10,720
Nooo!

1263
01:20:10,720 --> 01:20:13,300
Aaah!

1264
01:20:13,300 --> 01:20:13,980
Aaah!

1265
01:20:16,500 --> 01:20:17,260
Aaah!

1266
01:20:17,260 --> 01:20:18,760
Aaah!

1267
01:20:18,760 --> 01:20:20,220
Aaah!

1268
01:20:26,460 --> 01:20:28,320
The tornado's being blown
off course by the wind!

1269
01:20:28,320 --> 01:20:30,220
Listen up, Joes!

1270
01:20:30,380 --> 01:20:31,740
Hurry up and do something!

1271
01:20:31,960 --> 01:20:33,720
How am I supposed to do something?!

1272
01:20:34,140 --> 01:20:36,520
Hey! Honda! Get over here, quick!

1273
01:20:36,720 --> 01:20:38,700
Yeah, yeah, got it!

1274
01:20:41,740 --> 01:20:46,380
Aaaaah!
I'm coming now, alright, got it, right?

1275
01:20:46,380 --> 01:20:48,700
Aaaaaah!

1276
01:20:48,700 --> 01:20:52,960
Aaaaaah! The tornado has made landfall!

1277
01:20:53,400 --> 01:20:58,040
From there, it'll be fine. I'll take care of it right away,
so, well then,

1278
01:20:58,480 --> 01:21:00,340
Four of them, right?

1279
01:21:00,340 --> 01:21:05,640
Aaaaaah! Did you hit that tornado or what?

1280
01:21:13,040 --> 01:21:18,620
The disc-shaped weapon that appeared in Tokyo
Bay destroyed Rainbow Bridge with a tornado,

1281
01:21:18,620 --> 01:21:20,760
and it's heading from behind
the island toward the city center.

1282
01:21:20,760 --> 01:21:27,520
Boss, if we get any closer to that tornado,
we'll just get blown away.

1283
01:21:27,520 --> 01:21:28,160
Come on.

1284
01:21:31,440 --> 01:21:35,580
That's it! Honda!
Get ahead of it and head for Tokyo Tower!

1285
01:21:35,840 --> 01:21:36,780
Tokyo Tower?

1286
01:21:37,060 --> 01:21:37,960
Just go!

1287
01:21:38,420 --> 01:21:40,060
Alright! My heart's pounding!

1288
01:21:48,200 --> 01:21:48,920
Go!

1289
01:21:49,640 --> 01:21:50,400
Here I go!

1290
01:21:51,760 --> 01:21:54,800
Yaaah! Yaaah! Yaaah! Yaaah!
Yaaah! Yaaah! Yaaah! Yaaah!

1291
01:22:00,940 --> 01:22:01,760
Die!

1292
01:22:02,790 --> 01:22:03,660
Die!

1293
01:22:03,660 --> 01:22:06,500
Whaaaaat

1294
01:22:06,500 --> 01:22:07,020
Whaaaaat

1295
01:22:07,020 --> 01:22:07,420
Whaaaaat

1296
01:22:07,420 --> 01:22:07,820
Whaaaaat

1297
01:22:07,820 --> 01:22:08,420
Whaaaaat

1298
01:22:18,320 --> 01:22:19,860
There it is!

1299
01:22:19,860 --> 01:22:21,240
Eeeeeeeh!

1300
01:22:22,840 --> 01:22:23,820
Eeeeeeeh!

1301
01:22:23,820 --> 01:22:24,440
Eeeeeeeh!

1302
01:22:25,440 --> 01:22:26,340
Yay!

1303
01:22:28,100 --> 01:22:29,240
Whoa, it's flying!

1304
01:22:30,260 --> 01:22:31,880
Uh-oh!

1305
01:22:35,700 --> 01:22:37,900
We did it! Yes!

1306
01:22:38,680 --> 01:22:41,720
Yes! Ryotsu has boarded the Hiryumaru!

1307
01:22:41,940 --> 01:22:43,100
Well done, Ryotsu!

1308
01:22:43,500 --> 01:22:45,056
Good. Now I can relax.

1309
01:22:45,106 --> 01:22:47,880
Our brave officers have boarded the disc!

1310
01:22:48,340 --> 01:22:51,760
I'll bring the Hiryumaru back to the sea!
Leave it to me!

1311
01:22:53,240 --> 01:22:54,060
Swish!

1312
01:22:58,260 --> 01:23:00,080
Mister! It's not this way!

1313
01:23:00,080 --> 01:23:03,080
Eeeeeeeh!

1314
01:23:13,060 --> 01:23:15,660
Aaaaaaah!

1315
01:23:15,660 --> 01:23:15,700
Aaaaaaah!

1316
01:23:20,120 --> 01:23:22,480
Damn, it's this way!

1317
01:23:35,740 --> 01:23:39,060
Yikes! Now it's blown up
the National Diet Building!

1318
01:23:39,620 --> 01:23:42,840
That idiot,
is he planning to wreck all of Tokyo?

1319
01:23:43,260 --> 01:23:46,960
R-r-right, well, this is

1320
01:23:46,960 --> 01:23:50,140
Hello? Right, hello?

1321
01:23:50,140 --> 01:23:53,360
Okay, we've got to get it
back toward the sea somehow!

1322
01:24:06,660 --> 01:24:08,180
The Shiosite is...

1323
01:24:11,060 --> 01:24:13,980
Compared to this, Tiger was still better!

1324
01:24:14,540 --> 01:24:18,080
Chief, what on earth are you...

1325
01:24:18,740 --> 01:24:20,940
It's the surface, Ohara-kun!

1326
01:24:26,280 --> 01:24:28,260
What a wind this is!

1327
01:24:28,260 --> 01:24:28,580
Aaagh!

1328
01:24:32,920 --> 01:24:33,320
Rain?

1329
01:24:35,820 --> 01:24:39,640
Ryotsu, what are you doing?
Stop that tornado quickly!

1330
01:24:39,640 --> 01:24:41,700
We can't stop it.

1331
01:24:41,700 --> 01:24:47,500
According to Tappei, it's set to keep
sucking in air until it self-destructs.

1332
01:24:47,500 --> 01:24:49,260
What? Self-destruct?

1333
01:24:49,440 --> 01:24:51,980
Damn it, Ryotsu, get out quickly!

1334
01:24:51,980 --> 01:24:58,260
But if I don't hold down the control stick like this,
the wind from the sea will push the tornado back!

1335
01:24:59,520 --> 01:25:02,280
That's bad. Ryotsu, keep holding it down!

1336
01:25:03,780 --> 01:25:04,380
Ōtsu is...

1337
01:25:09,360 --> 01:25:10,300
This is bad.

1338
01:25:10,300 --> 01:25:11,920
A typhoon is approaching.

1339
01:25:11,920 --> 01:25:13,280
A typhoon, you say?

1340
01:25:13,280 --> 01:25:15,760
It's that super-massive typhoon.

1341
01:25:15,760 --> 01:25:16,260
What?

1342
01:25:16,260 --> 01:25:18,040
Ryo-chan is...

1343
01:25:18,460 --> 01:25:20,040
What's happening with the Hiryumaru?

1344
01:25:20,440 --> 01:25:23,000
Ryotsu is piloting the Hiryumaru.

1345
01:25:23,000 --> 01:25:26,000
And they say it's going to
self-destruct any moment now.

1346
01:25:27,640 --> 01:25:30,760
The super-massive typhoon that
has been approaching since yesterday

1347
01:25:30,760 --> 01:25:33,720
is about to hit the metropolitan
area head-on at breakneck speed.

1348
01:25:34,120 --> 01:25:36,900
If heavy rain causes rivers to swell,

1349
01:25:36,900 --> 01:25:39,360
many areas may be flooded,

1350
01:25:39,360 --> 01:25:43,340
and since lifelines such as roads
have been cut off by the tornado,

1351
01:25:43,340 --> 01:25:46,200
the damage could spread even further.

1352
01:25:49,780 --> 01:25:51,800
Hurry up and take it down!

1353
01:25:55,140 --> 01:25:55,807
Ohara-kun,

1354
01:25:55,857 --> 01:25:59,980
if we get hit directly by this typhoon,
we're in big trouble.

1355
01:26:00,540 --> 01:26:04,300
A typhoon on top of a tornado?
What on earth are we supposed to do?

1356
01:26:07,040 --> 01:26:10,960
Five minutes until detonation.
Evacuate immediately.

1357
01:26:11,760 --> 01:26:14,100
What? It's going to explode in five minutes?

1358
01:26:14,600 --> 01:26:15,560
What did you say?

1359
01:26:16,300 --> 01:26:19,360
Ryotsu, that's enough. Get out of there now.

1360
01:26:19,980 --> 01:26:23,160
But if I run away from the Hiryumaru now,

1361
01:26:35,920 --> 01:26:38,720
Target lock acquired, target insufficient.

1362
01:26:42,740 --> 01:26:44,760
Target... I see.

1363
01:26:45,600 --> 01:26:49,220
Chief, I'll use the Hiryumaru
to wipe out the typhoon.

1364
01:26:50,200 --> 01:26:50,920
What?

1365
01:26:50,920 --> 01:26:54,020
The Hiryumaru was originally
built for exactly that purpose.

1366
01:26:54,780 --> 01:26:59,480
If we follow its original functions, the
Hiryumaru should be able to avoid self-destructing.

1367
01:26:59,900 --> 01:27:02,960
It's dangerous. We don't know if it'll work.

1368
01:27:02,960 --> 01:27:06,020
Regardless, I believe in Tappei's invention.

1369
01:27:07,560 --> 01:27:12,460
Ryo-chan, you might be wiped
out before the typhoon is!

1370
01:27:13,120 --> 01:27:14,800
Ryo-san, I don't want you to die!

1371
01:27:15,240 --> 01:27:18,780
Don't worry.
The Hiryumaru isn't a weapon of destruction.

1372
01:27:19,780 --> 01:27:22,380
I'll prove it on behalf of everyone.

1373
01:27:23,280 --> 01:27:24,000
Yone-san...

1374
01:27:24,780 --> 01:27:26,820
Alright, Tappei, watch me!

1375
01:28:04,500 --> 01:28:05,780
It's gone quiet.

1376
01:28:05,780 --> 01:28:07,060
Target reached.

1377
01:28:07,060 --> 01:28:09,740
Activate the storm diffuser.

1378
01:28:09,740 --> 01:28:12,040
"Activate it," they say.

1379
01:28:12,040 --> 01:28:15,720
Pressure limit explosion in 20 seconds.

1380
01:28:15,720 --> 01:28:17,320
What do we do?

1381
01:28:17,320 --> 01:28:19,480
Explosion in 15 seconds.

1382
01:28:22,800 --> 01:28:23,860
This is it.

1383
01:28:25,660 --> 01:28:26,760
We're out of time.

1384
01:28:29,380 --> 01:28:30,880
It's now or never.

1385
01:28:30,880 --> 01:28:33,880
Storm diffuser activated.

1386
01:29:37,480 --> 01:29:38,980
We're saved!

1387
01:29:38,980 --> 01:29:42,560
The typhoon's gone!

1388
01:29:42,560 --> 01:29:44,300
Ryo-san did it!

1389
01:30:10,020 --> 01:30:11,160
Yay!

1390
01:30:12,420 --> 01:30:13,840
Yay!

1391
01:30:25,800 --> 01:30:32,000
We did it, we really did!
The Hiryumaru wiped out the typhoon!

1392
01:30:32,760 --> 01:30:34,340
I knew it. I should've said so.

1393
01:30:34,340 --> 01:30:38,160
Yay! We did it!

1394
01:30:42,580 --> 01:30:43,020
Me?

1395
01:30:55,780 --> 01:30:56,620
We have to go save them!

1396
01:31:03,800 --> 01:31:05,440
I thought I was going to die.

1397
01:31:06,200 --> 01:31:10,420
Hey! Over here!

1398
01:31:25,780 --> 01:31:26,960
Well done!

1399
01:31:27,100 --> 01:31:28,700
Ryo-chan, I'm so glad you're here!

1400
01:31:29,000 --> 01:31:30,540
Ryo-san, you're amazing!

1401
01:31:36,680 --> 01:31:37,620
Mina...

1402
01:31:38,660 --> 01:31:39,740
Where's Tappei?

1403
01:31:39,960 --> 01:31:42,040
Well, that's...

1404
01:31:58,320 --> 01:31:59,400
Ah

1405
01:31:59,400 --> 01:31:59,900
Ah

1406
01:31:59,900 --> 01:32:00,540
Ah

1407
01:32:00,540 --> 01:32:01,820
Ah

1408
01:32:01,820 --> 01:32:02,980
Ah

1409
01:32:02,980 --> 01:32:04,620
Ah

1410
01:32:04,620 --> 01:32:05,200
Ah

1411
01:32:05,200 --> 01:32:05,320
Ah

1412
01:32:05,320 --> 01:32:05,720
Ah

1413
01:32:05,720 --> 01:32:07,300
Ah

1414
01:32:31,020 --> 01:32:32,520
Mina, where's Papa?

1415
01:32:33,260 --> 01:32:34,740
Don't say anything more.

1416
01:32:34,740 --> 01:32:36,760
I'm sorry, Papa.

1417
01:32:37,680 --> 01:32:38,400
Mina

1418
01:32:57,380 --> 01:32:58,077
Listen well,

1419
01:32:58,127 --> 01:33:01,680
you've completely ruined my plan.

1420
01:33:01,680 --> 01:33:03,660
Taiga, you're still alive?

1421
01:33:03,660 --> 01:33:07,140
Now I'll send all of you straight to hell.

1422
01:33:08,520 --> 01:33:14,260
Pankichi!

1423
01:33:14,260 --> 01:33:15,140
Ryo-san!

1424
01:33:16,780 --> 01:33:17,900
Damn it!

1425
01:33:17,900 --> 01:33:20,120
Aaaaaah!

1426
01:33:20,120 --> 01:33:21,480
Aaaaaah!

1427
01:33:21,480 --> 01:33:21,900
Aaaaaah!

1428
01:33:21,900 --> 01:33:28,500
Eeeeeeh!

1429
01:33:34,580 --> 01:33:38,320
Feels like I've seen
this kind of scene before.

1430
01:33:38,660 --> 01:33:39,820
Aaaaaah!

1431
01:33:39,820 --> 01:33:41,240
That guy! Move, move!

1432
01:33:41,720 --> 01:33:42,540
Do it!

1433
01:33:43,300 --> 01:33:45,700
Kankichi, this guy... could he be...

1434
01:33:46,660 --> 01:33:48,900
Jikijō! You'll regret this!

1435
01:33:49,580 --> 01:33:51,265
Whoa! Could it be...

1436
01:33:51,315 --> 01:33:54,440
The bully I beat up when I was a kid?

1437
01:33:54,840 --> 01:33:58,120
So that's the one humiliation
we went through together?

1438
01:33:58,480 --> 01:34:02,460
What a twist of fate!

1439
01:34:30,840 --> 01:34:36,380
Wanting to see you,
unable to meet, longing to see you

1440
01:34:37,520 --> 01:34:42,380
Gazing up at the stars in the night sky

1441
01:34:44,200 --> 01:34:50,820
Even their shining that
seems to sit side by side

1442
01:34:50,820 --> 01:34:54,280
Though in truth we are apart

1443
01:34:54,280 --> 01:34:56,760
Tappei, you were threatened

1444
01:34:56,760 --> 01:34:59,200
and had no choice but
to pilot the Hiryumaru.

1445
01:34:59,640 --> 01:35:01,980
You're sure to be found not guilty in court.

1446
01:35:02,600 --> 01:35:03,260
Kankichi.

1447
01:35:03,260 --> 01:35:05,280
We'll cheer you on too.

1448
01:35:05,280 --> 01:35:07,120
It'll be absolutely fine.

1449
01:35:07,120 --> 01:35:08,140
That's right.

1450
01:35:08,580 --> 01:35:09,420
Please do your best.

1451
01:35:09,420 --> 01:35:11,260
For Mina-chan's sake, too.

1452
01:35:15,980 --> 01:35:16,380
Thank you very much.

1453
01:35:22,580 --> 01:35:22,980
Everyone,

1454
01:35:24,480 --> 01:35:25,880
come on, Kankichi.

1455
01:35:27,960 --> 01:35:28,900
That's...

1456
01:35:30,500 --> 01:35:32,480
Isn't that the sushi
boat from Chō Kanta Sushi?

1457
01:35:33,160 --> 01:35:36,040
Kankichi! Thank you for protecting the town!

1458
01:35:36,540 --> 01:35:38,380
Kankichi really is amazing, after all.

1459
01:35:39,060 --> 01:35:41,180
This is the Agarga from Chō Kanta Sushi.

1460
01:35:41,180 --> 01:35:43,240
Don't hold back, go ahead and eat.

1461
01:35:43,980 --> 01:35:45,200
Thanks, Kebalt.

1462
01:35:45,200 --> 01:35:47,980
Matoi and Lemon, come over here too.

1463
01:35:48,520 --> 01:35:49,660
Alright, this is bad.

1464
01:35:52,220 --> 01:35:52,860
This is bad.

1465
01:35:53,380 --> 01:35:55,300
We've got two Kankichis here.

1466
01:35:55,300 --> 01:35:56,040
Aaaaaah!

1467
01:36:01,040 --> 01:36:05,440
Everyone, well then,
tonight it's the Playcorder...

1468
01:36:06,520 --> 01:36:06,980
me

1469
01:36:19,880 --> 01:36:23,740
By the way, Tappei,
could you build me a UFO?

1470
01:36:24,560 --> 01:36:27,172
With one of those,
I could make a good business of it.

1471
01:36:27,222 --> 01:36:29,220
Of course, we'll split the profits.

1472
01:36:29,340 --> 01:36:30,600
Hey, Ryutsu!

1473
01:36:31,420 --> 01:36:32,460
P-p-pecha!

1474
01:36:32,680 --> 01:36:36,420
You're at it again, scheming up
some worthless moneymaking nonsense.

1475
01:36:36,700 --> 01:36:38,340
No well, this is...

1476
01:36:38,800 --> 01:36:41,340
Today I'm going to
knock some sense into you.

1477
01:36:41,380 --> 01:36:42,320
Sorry!

1478
01:36:42,600 --> 01:36:43,280
Hey, wait!

1479
01:36:43,720 --> 01:36:44,680
N-no, stop!

1480
01:36:44,980 --> 01:36:45,600
Wait!

1481
01:36:46,040 --> 01:36:46,640
Wait!

1482
01:36:46,640 --> 01:36:46,940
Wait!

1483
01:36:47,020 --> 01:36:47,940
Wait!

1484
01:37:09,560 --> 01:37:10,520
Aaargh!

1485
01:37:11,220 --> 01:37:13,620
W-wait, w-wait, wait!

1486
01:37:13,860 --> 01:37:15,820
Real aliens!?

1487
01:37:15,820 --> 01:37:16,500
Whoa!

1488
01:37:16,820 --> 01:37:19,100
Where do you plan to take us!?

1489
01:37:20,280 --> 01:37:21,800
Help us!

1490
01:37:34,660 --> 01:37:41,380
If you're a man, break out of your shell.

1491
01:37:41,380 --> 01:37:43,980
You're a man.

1492
01:37:44,740 --> 01:37:47,700
Tears that speak through your back.

1493
01:38:04,920 --> 01:38:11,300
Sorry for being stubborn,
but there are things I won't give up.

1494
01:38:11,740 --> 01:38:18,000
Selfish of me, I know,
but there's a road you can't turn back from.

1495
01:38:18,000 --> 01:38:24,280
More than kindness, more than words,

1496
01:38:25,060 --> 01:38:30,520
by protecting a small love.

1497
01:38:30,520 --> 01:38:31,100
Container

1498
01:38:31,100 --> 01:38:33,220
Container

1499
01:38:33,220 --> 01:38:34,480
Container

1500
01:38:34,480 --> 01:38:35,480
Container

1501
01:38:35,480 --> 01:38:38,800
If you're more of a man than just winning,

1502
01:38:40,410 --> 01:38:43,000
break through your shell!

1503
01:38:43,520 --> 01:38:45,660
You're a man.

1504
01:38:46,520 --> 01:38:49,520
Let your back speak, and your tears.

1505
01:38:55,780 --> 01:39:03,020
Sorry for being mean, I'm just embarrassed.

1506
01:39:03,580 --> 01:39:09,700
Sorry for being lonely,
when we finally reach it,

1507
01:39:09,700 --> 01:39:15,640
the rainbow visible beyond the rain

1508
01:39:16,700 --> 01:39:22,340
I'll catch it with these arms.

1509
01:39:23,680 --> 01:39:24,280
Here,

1510
01:39:26,700 --> 01:39:30,540
if you're a man from Katsushika,

1511
01:39:31,680 --> 01:39:34,580
show them a dream.

1512
01:39:34,580 --> 01:39:41,280
If you're a man, break out of your shell!

1513
01:39:41,280 --> 01:39:43,900
That's manly.

1514
01:39:44,560 --> 01:39:47,700
Tears that speak through your back,

1515
01:39:47,700 --> 01:39:51,200
tears that speak from the heart.

1516
01:40:04,580 --> 01:40:05,880
Yeah!

